[4739]={o="Speak to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens."},
[4740]={o="Find and slay the murloc known as Murkdeep. &nbsp;The creature is thought to be defending the murloc huts south of Auberdine along the water. Report the death of Murkdeep to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.",r={"Murkdeep (1)"},s="WANTED: Murkdeep!",e="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea"},
[4741]={o="Trull Failbane in Felwood wants you to hunt 13 Moontouched Owlbeasts.",r={"Moontouched Owlbeast (13)"}},
[4742]={o="Find the three gemstones of command: The Gemstone of Smolderthorn, Gemstone of Spirestone, and Gemstone of Bloodaxe. Return them, along with the Unadorned Seal of Ascension, to Vaelan. The Generals, as told to you by Vaelan, are: War Master Voone of the Smolderthorn; Highlord Omokk of the Spirestone; and Overlord Wyrmthalak &nbsp;of the Bloodaxe.",r={"Gemstone of Spirestone (1)","Gemstone of Smolderthorn (1)","Gemstone of Bloodaxe (1)","Unadorned Seal of Ascension (1)"}},
[4743]={o="Travel to the Wyrmbog in Dustwallow Marsh. Find the ancient drake, Emberstrife and beat him without mercy until his will is broken. It is at that moment which you must place the Unforged Seal of Ascension before the great beast. You must then be quick to use the Orb of Draconic Energy on his weakened form and claim dominion over his mental faculties. Control the beast and force the Flames of the Black Dragonflight upon the Unforged Seal of Ascension!",r={"Forged Seal of Ascension (1)"}},
[4761]={o="Speak with Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine.",s="Terenthis",e="Thundris Windweaver"},
[4762]={o="Travel north of Auberdine to the first waterfall along the Cliffspring River and draw a sample from the pool there. Return to Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine with the Cliffspring River Sample.",r={"Cliffspring River Sample (1)"},s="Thundris Windweaver",e="Thundris Windweaver"},
[4763]={o="Fill the Empty Cleansing Bowl at the Auberdine Moonwell. Gather a sample of fruit, nut, and grain from the northern Blackwood furbolg camps. Mix the bowl and place it near the bonfire closest to the Cliffspring River at the northern camp, thus summoning the satyr corruptor. Take the Talisman of Corruption and bring it to Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine.",r={"Talisman of Corruption (1)","Blackwood Fruit Sample (1)","Blackwood Grain Sample (1)","Blackwood Nut Sample (1)"},s="Thundris Windweaver",e="Thundris Windweaver"},
[4764]={o="Bring Doomrigger's Clasp to Mayara Brightwing in the Burning Steppes.",r={"Doomrigger's Clasp (1)"}},
[4765]={o="Bring Ridgewell's Crate to Remington Ridgewell in Stormwind."},
[4766]={o="Speak with Mayara Brightwing in the Burning Steppes."},
[4767]={o="Bring 10 Highperch Wyvern Eggs to Elu in Freewind Post.",r={"Highperch Wyvern Egg (10)"}},
[4768]={o="Bring the Darkstone Tablet to Shadow Mage Vivian Lagrave in Kargath.",r={"Darkstone Tablet (1)"}},
[4769]={o="Speak with Shadowmage Vivian Lagrave."},
[4770]={o="Escort Pao'ka Swiftmountain from Highperch, and then talk to Motega Firemane in Whitereach Post.",r={"Escort Pao'ka from Highperch (1)"}},
[4771]={o="Place Dawn's Gambit in the Viewing Room of the Scholomance. &nbsp;Defeat Vectus, then return to Betina Bigglezink.",r={"Vectus (1)","Place Dawn's Gambit (1)"}},
[4781]={o="Bring a Gold Bar to Xizk Goodstitch in Stranglethorn Vale.",r={"Gold Bar (1)"}},
[4782]={o="Return to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens."},
[4783]={o="Bring 10 Vials of Hatefury Blood and 1 Lesser Infernal Stone to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.",r={"Vial of Hatefury Blood (10)","Lesser Infernal Stone (1)"}},
[4784]={o="Bring some Fine Gold Thread, 2 Smoldering Coals, and a Soul Shard to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.",r={"Fine Gold Thread (1)","Smoldering Coal (2)","Soul Shard (1)"}},
[4785]={o="Here you go, &lt;name&gt;. And please tell Menara we say hello. We expect great things of you. Perhaps when the Legion falls to its knees, your name will be spoken aloud and in praise of your power. I can't wait!"},
[4786]={o="Wait for Menara Voidrender to complete your robe and then speak to her again.",r={"Wait for Menara Voidrender to complete your item (1)"}},
[4787]={o="Bring the Ancient Egg to Yeh'kinya in Tanaris.",r={"Ancient Egg (1)"}},
[4788]={o="Bring the Fifth and Sixth Mosh'aru Tablets to Prospector Ironboot in Tanaris.",r={"Fifth Mosh'aru Tablet (1)","Sixth Mosh'aru Tablet (1)"}},
[4801]={o="In Winterspring, you will fight great cats called frostsabers. These beasts possess incredible speed an' cunning. If you wish ta gain the speed a' da frostsaber, bring me da E'ko you find from dem. Rememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.",r={"Frostsaber E'ko (3)"}},
[4802]={o="In Winterspring, you will fight misguided creatures known as da Winterfall furbolg. Through the wishes of their leader, dey have gained incredible strength. If you wish ta gain the power a' da Winterfall, bring me da E'ko you find from dem. Rememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.",r={"Winterfall E'ko (3)"}},
[4803]={o="In Winterspring, you will find large bears wit extremely thick hides. These Shardtooth bears gain much protection from what dey can withstand. If you wish ta gain the resistance against fire, bring me da E'ko you find from da Shardtooth. Rememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.",r={"Shardtooth E'ko (3)"}},
[4804]={o="In Winterspring, you will fight great flying creatures called da Chillwind. These beasts possess da power ta wield frost magics. If you wish ta gain resistance ta frost, bring me da E'ko you find from da Chillwind. Rememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.",r={"Chillwind E'ko (3)"}},
[4805]={o="In Winterspring, you will fight great creatures called da ice thistle yeti. These beasts move slowly, but dey are able to evade many blows from da protection their thick fur provides dem. If you wish ta gain da ability to dodge attacks, bring me da E'ko you find from dem. Rememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.",r={"Ice Thistle E'ko (3)"}},
[4806]={o="In Winterspring, you have fought da large ice giants called frostmaul. Sheer power and force is at their disposal. If you wish ta gain da force of da frostmaul, bring me da E'ko you find from dem. Rememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.",r={"Frostmaul E'ko (3)"}},
[4807]={o="In Winterspring, you will fight creatures of might dat seem to possess an innate magic ability. These wildkin can use strong magics. If you wish ta gain an increase in your intellect bring me da E'ko you find from any a' da owlbeasts you find der. Rememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.",r={"Wildkin E'ko (3)"}},
[4808]={o="Give Tinkee's Letter to Felnok Steelspring."},
[4809]={o="Bring 8 Uncracked Chillwind Horns to Felnok Steelspring.",r={"Uncracked Chillwind Horn (8)"}},
[4810]={o="Bring Felnok's Package to Tinkee Steamboil in the Burning Steppes."},
[4811]={o="Travel east of Auberdine and look for a large, red crystal along Darkshore's eastern mountain range. &nbsp;Report back what you find to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.",r={"(1)","Locate the large, red crystal on Darkshore's eastern mountain range (1)"},s="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea",e="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea"},
[4812]={o="Fill the Empty Water Tube at the Auberdine moonwell, and then investigate the red crystal along Darkshore's eastern mountain wall.",r={"Moonwell Water Tube (1)"},s="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea",e="Mysterious Red Crystal"},
[4813]={o="Report back what you have found to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.",s="Mysterious Red Crystal",e="Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea"},
[4821]={o="Return the Alien Egg to Hagar Lightninghoof in Freewind Post.",r={"Alien Egg (1)"}},
[4841]={o="Kill 12 Galak Scouts, 10 Galak Wranglers, and 6 Galak Windchasers, and then return to Cliffwatcher Longhorn in Freewind Post.",r={"Galak Scout (12)","Galak Wrangler (10)","Galak Windchaser (6)"}},
[4842]={o="Follow Donova Snowden's instructions, then report back.",r={"(1)","Discover Darkwhisper Gorge (1)"}},
[4861]={o="Locate Jaron Stoneshaper's wrecked camp and supplies in southern Winterspring."},
[4862]={o="Travel to Blackrock Spire and collect 15 Spire Spider Eggs for Kibler. By the sound of it, these eggs could be found near spiders.",r={"Spire Spider Egg (15)"}},
[4863]={o="Find Jaron Stoneshaper's wrecked wagon."},
[4864]={o="Pick up Jaron's Supplies from the snow, then find the wildkin that stole the amulet Jaron spoke of. Bring Jaron's Supplies and the Blue-feathered Amulet to Jaron Stoneshaper at the lodge in Winterspring.",r={"Jaron's Supplies (1)","Blue-feathered Amulet (1)"}},
[4865]={o="Report your findings to Motega Firemane."},
[4866]={o="In the heart of Blackrock Spire you will find Mother Smolderweb. Engage her and get her to poison you. Chances are good that you will have to kill her as well. Return to Ragged John when you are poisoned so that he can 'milk' you.",r={"Milked (1)"}},
[4867]={o="Read Warosh's Scroll. &nbsp;Bring Warosh's Mojo to Warosh.",r={"Warosh's Mojo (1)"}},
[4881]={o="Warn Kanati Greycloud at Whitereach Post of the plot to kill him."},
[4882]={o="Take the Blue-feathered Necklace to Trull Failbane at Bloodvenom Post."},
[4883]={o="Take the Blue-feathered Necklace to Nara Wildmane."},
[4901]={o="Protect Ranshalla while she attempts to reactivate the Altar of Elune. Report your findings to Erelas Ambersky in Rut'theran Village.",r={"Discover the secret of the Altar of Elune (1)"}},
[4902]={o="Speak with Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus."},
[4903]={o="Slay Highlord Omokk, War Master Voone, and Overlord Wyrmthalak. Recover Important Blackrock Documents. Return to Warlord Goretooth in Kargath when the mission has been accomplished.",r={"Overlord Wyrmthalak (1)","Highlord Omokk (1)","War Master Voone (1)","Important Blackrock Documents (1)"}},
[4904]={o="Escort Lakota Windsong from the Darkcloud Pinnacle, and then talk to Thalia Amberhide at Freewind Post.",r={"Escort Lakota Windsong from the Darkcloud Pinnacle. (1)"}},
[4906]={o="Eridan Bluewind in Felwood wants you to kill 8 Jadefire Hellcallers, 8 Jadefire Betrayers, 8 Jadefire Tricksters, and Xavaric. Return to Eridan when the task is completed.",r={"Jadefire Hellcaller (8)","Jadefire Betrayer (8)","Jadefire Trickster (8)","Xavaric (1)"}},
[4907]={o="Speak with Tinkee Steamboil."},
[4921]={o="Find Mankrik's wife and then return to him in the Crossroads.",r={"Find Mankrik's Wife (1)"}},
[4941]={o="Speak with Eitrigg in Orgrimmar. When you have discussed matters with Eitrigg, seek council from Thrall. You recall having seen Eitrigg in Thrall's chamber.",r={"Council with Eitrigg. (1)"}},
[4961]={o="Kill the Demon of the Orb, then speak with Tabetha.",r={"Demon of the Orb (1)"}},
[4962]={o="Take the Felhas Ruby and use it on one of the Felhounds found in Desolace. After successful, bring the Felhas Ruby and the Imprisoned Felhound Spirit back to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.",r={"Imprisoned Felhound Spirit (1)"}},
[4963]={o="Take the Infus Emerald and use it on one of the Infernals found in Desolace. After successful, bring the Infus Emerald and the Imprisoned Infernal Spirit back to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.",r={"Imprisoned Infernal Spirit (1)"}},
[4964]={o="Wait for Menara Voidrender to complete the Orb of Dar'Orahil and then speak to her again.",r={"Wait for Menara Voidrender to complete your item (1)"}},
[4965]={o="Speak to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens."},
[4966]={o="Protect Kanati Greycloud from the centaur attack.",r={"Protect Kanati Greycloud (1)"}},
[4967]={o="Speak to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens."},
[4968]={o="Speak to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens."},
[4969]={o="Speak to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens."},
[4970]={o="Collect 5 Shardtooth Meats and 5 Chillwind Meats for Rivern Frostwind in Winterspring.",r={"Shardtooth Meat (5)","Chillwind Meat (5)"}},
[4971]={o="Use the Temporal Displacer near one of Andorhal's silos and uncover Temporal Parasites. Slay 15 Temporal Parasites, and then return the Temporal Displacer to Chromie in the Andorhal Inn, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Temporal Parasite (15)"}},
[4972]={o="Locate 5 Andorhal Watches, found in lockboxes amongst the rubble of the city. &nbsp;Return with them to Chromie in the Andorhal Inn, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Andorhal Watch (5)"}},
[4973]={o="Locate 5 Andorhal Watches amongst the rubble of the city, and return with them to Chromie in the Andorhal Inn, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Andorhal Watch (5)"}},
[4974]={o="Travel to Blackrock Spire and slay Warchief Rend Blackhand. Take his head and return to Orgrimmar.",r={"Head of Rend Blackhand (1)"}},
[4975]={o="Wait for Menara Voidrender to complete the Orb of Noh'Orahil and then speak to her again.",r={"Wait for Menara Voidrender to complete your item (1)"}},
[4976]={o="Return the Cleansed Infernal Orb to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens."},
[4981]={o="Travel to Blackrock Spire and find out what happened to Bijou."},
[4982]={o="Find Bijou's Belongings and return them to her. You recall her mentioning that she stashed them on the bottom floor of the city.",r={"Bijou's Belongings (1)"}},
[4983]={o="Take Bijou's Reconnaissance Report back to Grandmaster Lexlort in Kargath."},
[4984]={o="Destroy 8 Diseased Wolves, and then return to Mulgris Deepriver at the Writhing Haunt, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Diseased Wolf (8)"}},
[4985]={o="Destroy 8 Diseased Grizzlies, and then return to Mulgris Deepriver at the Writhing Haunt, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Diseased Grizzly (8)"}},
[4986]={o="Based on the magic enchanted within the Glyphed Oaken Branch, its delivery to the Cenarion Circle in Darnassus is the next step the tauren druid sought. &nbsp;Seek one of the druids there for assistance."},
[4987]={o="Based on the magic enchanted within the Glyphed Oaken Branch, its delivery to the Cenarion Circle in Thunder Bluff is the next step the tauren druid sought. &nbsp;Seek one of the druids there for assistance."},
[5001]={o="Find Bijou's Belongings and return them to her. Good luck!",r={"Bijou's Belongings (1)"}},
[5002]={o="Travel to the Burning Steppes and give Bijou's Information to Marshal Maxwell."},
[5021]={o="The ramblings of the ghostly woman indicated that she needed a package delivered. &nbsp;She claimed that it was where her horse was. &nbsp;As to where the horse is or where the package was to be delivered - the ghost remains incomprehensible."},
[5022]={o="Check with the Royal Factors of Stormwind to learn the whereabouts of an Emma Felstone. &nbsp;There is usually a census officer located in City Hall."},
[5023]={o="Check with the Royal Overseers of the Undercity to learn the whereabouts of a Jeremiah Felstone. &nbsp;There is usually a census officer located near guild and tabard registration."},
[5041]={o="Find and return Crossroads' Supply Crates to Thork in the Barrens.",r={"Crossroads' Supply Crates (1)"}},
[5042]={o="I will need 4 blood shards if you wish Agamaggan's strength, &lt;race&gt;. Your foes will cower before your strength were you to be given this blessing. The Razormane's greatest warriors are infused with such power!",r={"Blood Shard (4)"}},
[5043]={o="My tribes greatest scouts are said to be unrivaled in their accuracy, and no rogue &lt;snort&gt; could measure up to their quickness in battle. Bring me 4 blood shards and I will make you even more agile than any quilboar born.",r={"Blood Shard (4)"}},
[5044]={o="The shaman and geomancers of the quilboar tribes &lt;snort&gt; call upon the strength of Agamaggan to help them in battle and in their rituals, &lt;race&gt;. If you too wish the added power of Agamaggan's blessing with your spells, then bring me 4 blood shards and Mangletooth will aid you.",r={"Blood Shard (4)"}},
[5045]={o="Warriors of all types &lt;snort&gt; have need of a strong spirit. It drives you to greater feats when all hope has been lost. This is not unknown to the &lt;snort&gt; Razormane. We are a spiritual tribe--we are more proud of our connection to Agamaggan than our prowess &lt;snort&gt; in battle. Bring me 4 blood shards and I will bless your spirit for battle. &lt;snort&gt;",r={"Blood Shard (4)"}},
[5046]={o="All those who &lt;snort&gt; enter battle have need of protection. Their bones must be strong. Their skin tough. &lt;snort&gt; My tribe knows this as well, and to add to the natural protection our quills and hide give us, &lt;snort&gt; we often call upon Agamaggan to protect us from harm before we go to war. Bring me 4 blood shards &lt;snort&gt; and I will grant you the same protection.",r={"Blood Shard (4)"}},
[5047]={o="Talk to Malyfous Darkhammer in Everlook."},
[5048]={o="Find Ol' Emma in Stormwind and see if she is in fact Emma Felstone. &nbsp;If she is, then perhaps she'd like the package Janice Felstone made for her."},
[5049]={o="Find Jeremiah Payson in the Undercity and see if he is in fact Jeremiah Felstone. &nbsp;If he is, then perhaps he'd like the package Janice Felstone made for him."},
[5050]={o="Return to Janice Felstone in Western Plaguelands her Good Luck Half-Charm."},
[5051]={o="Locate the other half of the Good Luck Charm somewhere on the Felstone Farm in Western Plaguelands and reassemble it. Give the Good Luck Charm to Janice Felstone on the Felstone Farm, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Good Luck Charm (1)","Good Luck Other-Half-Charm (1)"}},
[5052]={o="Bring a Blood Shard to Mangletooth in Camp Taurajo in the Barrens. Collect more Blood Shards if you want him to bless you with Agamaggan's power.",r={"Blood Shard (1)"}},
[5054]={o="Storm Shadowhoof at Everlook in Winterspring wants you to kill Ursius.",r={"Ursius (1)"}},
[5055]={o="Storm Shadowhoof at Everlook in Winterspring wants you to kill Brumeran.",r={"Brumeran (1)"}},
[5056]={o="Storm Shadowhoof at Everlook in Winterspring wants you to defeat Shy-Rotam.",r={"Shy-Rotam (1)","Sacred Frostsaber Meat (1)"}},
[5057]={o="Bring Storm Shadowhoof's Marker to Melor Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff."},
[5058]={o="A diary with yellowing pages lies open to the last entry: \"I don't know what's going to happen now that Harold's turned. &nbsp;It took everything out of me to drag him into the only place I could find that'd lock him up tight and hold him. &nbsp;I hid the key on me, and I pray it works... I hope I can get out of here, but I need money to do that. &nbsp;Our stuff's all in the cabinet I think... and now that I think about it, doesn't Harold keep the key on him? I'll rest on it, I'm dead tired now.\""},
[5059]={o="The door to the outhouse has begun to splinter at the edges of the frame as though it has been repeatedly and incessantly tried to be forced open. &nbsp;It is currently locked up tight from the outside of the outhouse. As you rattle the door, you hear a guttural moaning come from inside! &nbsp;Whatever is inside there, it certainly does not sound friendly.",r={"Dalson Outhouse Key (1)"}},
[5060]={o="An extremely sturdy cabinet stands before you, securely fastened shut by a built-in lock. &nbsp;The front of the cabinet is deeply scratched and marked. &nbsp;This could be surmised as being from numerous and violent failed attempts to reveal whatever secrets the cabinet currently obfuscates from view. If you are going to open this cabinet, you will need to find the key.",r={"Dalson Cabinet Key (1)"}},
[5061]={o="Return to Darnassus and show Mathrengyl Bearwalker the Pendant of the Sea Lion.",s="Dendrite Starblaze",e="Mathrengyl Bearwalker"},
[5062]={o="Gather 10 bushels of Incendia Agave, and then consult Magatha Grimtotem on Elder Rise in Thunderbluff.",r={"Incendia Agave (10)"}},
[5063]={o="In order to create the Cap of the Scarlet Savant, you will be required to bring the following items back to Malyfous Darkhammer: 1 Pristine Hide of the Beast; 5 Frayed Abomination Stitchings; 8 Arcane Crystals; 5 Enchanted Scarlet Thread. You will also be required to pay 50 gold pieces for the crafting of the item.",r={"Frayed Abomination Stitching (5)","Arcane Crystal (8)","Enchanted Scarlet Thread (5)","Money: 50 &nbsp; (1)"}},
[5064]={o="Locate and retrieve the three Secret Notes in Darkcloud Pinnacle",r={"Secret Note #1 (1)","Secret Note #2 (1)","Secret Note #3 (1)"}},
[5065]={o="Bring the Third and Fourth Mosh'aru Tablets to Prospector Ironboot in Tanaris.",r={"Third Mosh'aru Tablet (1)","Fourth Mosh'aru Tablet (1)"}},
[5066]={o="Seek out Commander Ashlam Valorfist. &nbsp;His base camp is located at Chillwind Camp, north of the Alterac Mountains."},
[5067]={o="In order to create the Leggings of Arcana, you will be required to bring the following items back to Malyfous Darkhammer: 1 Pristine Hide of the Beast; 5 Frayed Abomination Stitchings; 5 Arcanite Bars; 5 Frostwhisper's Embalming Fluid. You will also be required to pay 50 gold pieces for the crafting of the item.",r={"Frayed Abomination Stitching (5)","Arcanite Bar (5)","Frostwhisper's Embalming Fluid (5)","Money: 50 &nbsp; (1)"}},
[5068]={o="In order to create the Breastplate of Bloodthirst, you will be required to bring the following items back to Malyfous Darkhammer: 1 Pristine Hide of the Beast; 10 Frayed Abomination Stitchings; 5 Arcanite Bars; 5 Skin of Shadow. You will also be required to pay 50 gold pieces for the crafting of the item.",r={"Frayed Abomination Stitching (10)","Arcanite Bar (5)","Skin of Shadow (5)","Money: 50 &nbsp; (1)"}},
[5081]={o="Travel to Blackrock Spire and destroy War Master Voone, Highlord Omokk, and Overlord Wyrmthalak. Return to Marshal Maxwell when the job is done.",r={"War Master Voone (1)","Highlord Omokk (1)","Overlord Wyrmthalak (1)"}},
[5082]={o="Donova Snowden in Winterspring wants you to kill 8 Winterfall Pathfinders, 8 Winterfall Den Watchers, and 8 Winterfall Totemics.",r={"Winterfall Pathfinder (8)","Winterfall Den Watcher (8)","Winterfall Totemic (8)"}},
[5083]={o="Bring the Empty Firewater Flask to Donova Snowden in Winterspring."},
[5084]={o="Search the Deadwood furbolg camp in northern Felwood for a clue."},
[5085]={o="Report back to Donova Snowden with your findings."},
[5086]={o="Collect 3 Toxic Horror Droplets for Donova Snowden in Winterspring.",r={"Toxic Horror Droplet (3)"}},
[5087]={o="Find the Winterfall Runners and stop them from delivering their shipment to Winterfall Village.",r={"Winterfall Crate (1)"}},
[5088]={o="Slay Arikara. Bring her remains and the Incendia powder to Motega Firemane in Whitereach Post as proof of your deed.",r={"Arikara Serpent Skin (1)","Light the Sacred Fire of Life (1)"}},
[5089]={o="Take General Drakkisath's Command to Marshal Maxwell in Burning Steppes."},
[5090]={o="Seek out Commander Ashlam Valorfist. &nbsp;His base camp is located at Chillwind Camp, north of the Alterac Mountains."},
[5091]={o="Seek out Commander Ashlam Valorfist. &nbsp;His base camp is located at Chillwind Camp, north of the Alterac Mountains."},
[5092]={o="Kill 10 Skeletal Flayers and 10 Slavering Ghouls in Sorrow Hill. Return to Commander Ashlam Valorfist at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Skeletal Flayer (10)","Slavering Ghoul (10)"}},
[5093]={o="Seek out High Executor Derrington. &nbsp;His base camp is located at the Bulwark, east of Tirisfal Glade and the Undercity."},
[5094]={o="Seek out High Executor Derrington. &nbsp;His base camp is located at the Bulwark, east of Tirisfal Glade and the Undercity."},
[5095]={o="Seek out High Executor Derrington. &nbsp;His base camp is located at the Bulwark, east of Tirisfal Glades and the Undercity."},
[5096]={o="Proceed to the Scarlet Crusade's base camp between Felstone Field and Dalson's Tears and destroy their command tent. Place the Scourge banner at the camp, and then return to High Executor Derrington at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Flame in a Bottle (1)","Destroy the command tent and plant the Scourge banner in the camp (1)"}},
[5097]={o="Using the Beacon Torch, mark each tower in Andorhal; you will need to stand in the doorway of the tower to successfully mark it. Once all four towers are marked, return the Beacon Torch to Commander Ashlam Valorfist in Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Tower One marked (1)","Tower Two marked (1)","Tower Three marked (1)","Tower Four marked (1)"}},
[5098]={o="Using the Beacon Torch, mark each tower in Andorhal; you will need to stand in the doorway of the tower to successfully mark it. Once all four towers are marked, return the Beacon Torch to High Executor Derrington at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Tower One marked (1)","Tower Two marked (1)","Tower Three marked (1)","Tower Four marked (1)"}},
[5101]={o="Kill 6 sheep for Benny and then run like hell! Just kidding... about the running part.",r={"Sheep (6)"}},
[5102]={o="Travel to Blackrock Spire and destroy General Drakkisath. Return to Marshal Maxwell when the job is done.",r={"General Drakkisath (1)"}},
[5103]={o="Someone in this world must know what to do with these gauntlets. Good luck!"},
[5121]={o="Donova Snowden in Winterspring wants you to defeat High Chief Winterfall.",r={"High Chief Winterfall (1)"}},
[5122]={o="The power of this chapel gives me the strength to resist the corruption in my heart. &nbsp;If I leave it, I will become a death knight. &nbsp; But there is a medallion, the medallion of faith, that will give me the strength I need to leave. Please, &lt;name&gt;, retrieve the medallion. &nbsp;It is guarded by Malor the Zealous, a crazed member of the Scarlet Brotherhood who resides deep in the Scarlet Bastion in western Stratholme.",r={"Medallion of Faith (1)"}},
[5123]={o="Bring the Crudely-written Log to Donova Snowden in Winterspring."},
[5124]={o="Bring Malyfous Darkhammer 6 Enchanted Thorium Bars, 2 Essence of Fire, and 4 Star Rubies. You will also need to turn in your Unfired Plate Gauntlets.",r={"Unfired Plate Gauntlets (1)","Enchanted Thorium Bar (6)","Essence of Fire (2)","Star Ruby (4)"}},
[5125]={o="&lt;name&gt;, I am dying... but my soul is saved. &nbsp;For that, I owe you more than words can say. &nbsp;Please, take this... and fight on, brave &lt;class&gt;!"},
[5126]={o="Speak with Lorax. Listen to what he has to say.",r={"Listen to Lorax's Tale (1)"}},
[5127]={o="Travel to Blackrock Spire and find Goraluk Anvilcrack. Slay him and then use the Blood Stained Pike upon his corpse. After his soul has been siphoned, the pike will be Soul Stained. You must also find the Unforged Rune Covered Breastplate. Return both the Soul Stained Pike and the Unforged Rune Covered Breastplate to Lorax in Winterspring.",r={"Soul Stained Pike (1)","Unforged Rune Covered Breastplate (1)"}},
[5128]={o="Take the Crudely-written Log to Kelek Skykeeper in southern Felwood."},
[5141]={o="Bring 2 Tough Scorpid Breastplates, 2 Tough Scorpid Gloves, and 10 Worn Dragonscales to Peter Galen in Azshara. Completing this quest will give you access to the Dragonscale Leatherworking arts. The completion of this quest will prevent you from learning Elemental Leatherworking and Tribal Leatherworking; be sure this is the path you wish to follow before doing so.",r={"Tough Scorpid Breastplate (2)","Tough Scorpid Gloves (2)","Worn Dragonscale (10)"}},
[5142]={o="Find Pamela Redpath."},
[5143]={o="Bring a Wild Leather Vest and a Wild Leather Helmet to Caryssia Moonhunter in Feralas. Completing this quest will give you access to the Tribal Leatherworking arts. The completion of this quest will prevent you from learning Dragonscale Leatherworking and Elemental Leatherworking; be sure this is the path you wish to follow before doing so.",r={"Wild Leather Vest (1)","Wild Leather Helmet (1)"}},
[5144]={o="Bring 2 Heart of Fire, 2 Globe of Water, 2 Core of Earth, and 2 Breath of Wind to Sarah Tanner in Searing Gorge. Completing this quest will give you access to the Elemental Leatherworking arts. The completion of this quest will prevent you from learning Dragonscale Leatherworking and Tribal Leatherworking; be sure this is the path you wish to follow before doing so.",r={"Heart of Fire (2)","Globe of Water (2)","Core of Earth (2)","Breath of Wind (2)"}},
[5145]={o="Bring 2 Tough Scorpid Breastplates, 2 Tough Scorpid Gloves, and 10 Worn Dragonscales to Thorkaf Dragoneye in the Badlands. Completing this quest will give you access to the Dragonscale Leatherworking arts. The completion of this quest will prevent you from learning Elemental Leatherworking and Tribal Leatherworking; be sure this is the path you wish to follow before doing so.",r={"Tough Scorpid Breastplate (2)","Tough Scorpid Gloves (2)","Worn Dragonscale (10)"}},
[5146]={o="Bring 2 Heart of Fire, 2 Globe of Water, 2 Core of Earth, and 2 Breath of Wind to Brumn Winterhoof in the Arathi Mountains. Completing this quest will give you access to the Elemental Leatherworking arts. The completion of this quest will prevent you from learning Dragonscale Leatherworking and Tribal Leatherworking; be sure this is the path you wish to follow before doing so.",r={"Heart of Fire (2)","Globe of Water (2)","Core of Earth (2)","Breath of Wind (2)"}},
[5147]={o="Slay Arnak Grimtotem and bring proof of your deed to Cliffwatcher Longhorn in Freewind Post.",r={"Arnak's Hoof (1)"}},
[5148]={o="Bring a Wild Leather Vest and a Wild Leather Helmet to Se'Jib in Stranglethorn Vale. Completing this quest will give you access to the Tribal Leatherworking arts. The completion of this quest will prevent you from learning Dragonscale Leatherworking and Elemental Leatherworking; be sure this is the path you wish to follow before doing so.",r={"Wild Leather Vest (1)","Wild Leather Helmet (1)"}},
[5149]={o="Find Pamela's doll.",r={"Pamela's Doll (1)","Pamela's Doll's Head (1)","Pamela's Doll's Left Side (1)","Pamela's Doll's Right Side (1)"}},
[5150]={o="Dadanga looks up at you as you approach her. She seems to be hoping for something... She's probably hungry! There's got to be something growing in the crater that would be just the perfect snack for a large herbivore. Dadanga's a big girl; whatever you bring her, there would need to be a lot of it!",r={"Bloodpetal Sprout (15)"}},
[5151]={o="Slay the beast and bring back the Hypercapacitor Gizmo and Panther Cage Key to Wizlo Bearingshiner.",r={"Hypercapacitor Gizmo (1)"}},
[5152]={o="Speak with Marlene, south of the Ruins of Andorhal."},
[5153]={o="Bring Joseph's Wedding Ring to Chromie.",r={"Joseph's Wedding Ring (1)"}},
[5154]={o="Bring the Annals of Darrowshire to Chromie in Andorhal.",r={"Annals of Darrowshire (1)"}},
[5155]={o="Enter Jaedenar and slay 4 Jaedenar Hounds, 4 Jaedenar Guardsmen, 6 Jaedenar Adepts, and 6 Jaedenar Cultists before returning to Greta Mosshoof in Felwood.",r={"Jaedenar Hound (4)","Jaedenar Guardian (4)","Jaedenar Adept (6)","Jaedenar Cultist (6)"}},
[5156]={o="Seek out and destroy 2 Entropic Beasts and 2 Entropic Horrors while exploring Shatter Scar Vale. After checking to see if the craters there are still filled with corrupt fel water, return to Taronn Redfeather in Felwood.",r={"Entropic Beast (2)","Entropic Horror (2)","(1)","Explore the craters in Shatter Scar Vale (1)"}},
[5157]={o="Take the Empty Canteen to the Moon Well in the center of Jaedenar and fill it before returning to Greta Mosshoof in Felwood.",r={"Corrupt Moonwell Water (1)"}},
[5158]={o="Take the Corrupt Moon Well Water to Islen Waterseer in the Barrens."},
[5159]={o="Take the Purified Moon Well Water to Greta Mosshoof in Felwood."},
[5160]={o="Travel to Winterspring and find Haleh. Give her Awbee's scale."},
[5161]={o="Speak with Haleh if you wish to continue."},
[5162]={o="Speak with Jeziba in the Plaguelands. He resides in Andorhal."},
[5163]={o="Take Umi's Mechanical Yeti and scare her friends with it: Legacki in Everlook (Winterspring) Sprinkle in Gadgetzan (Tanaris) Quixxil in Marshal's Refuge (Un'Goro Crater) When you are done, bring the Mechanical Yeti back to Umi.",r={"Scare Legacki (1)","Scare Sprinkle (1)","Scare Quixxil (1)"}},
[5164]={o="Read from the Catalogue of the Wayward."},
[5165]={o="Using the Purified Moon Well Water, douse the flames of the four braziers of protection within Shadow Hold in Felwood, then return to Greta Mosshoof in the Emerald Sanctuary.",r={"Extinguish the Brazier of Pain (1)","Extinguish the Brazier of Malice (1)","Extinguish the Brazier of Suffering (1)","Extinguish the Brazier of Hatred (1)"}},
[5166]={o="To forge the Breastplate of the Chromatic Flight, you will be required to bring the following items to Jeziba the 'Sculptor': 1 Chromatic Carapace. 10 Brilliant Chromatic Scales. 10 Blood of Heroes. 10 Frayed Abomination Stitchings.",r={"Brilliant Chromatic Scale (10)","Blood of Heroes (10)","Frayed Abomination Stitching (10)"}},
[5167]={o="To forge the Legplates of the Chromatic Defier, you will be required to bring the following items to Jeziba the 'Sculptor': 1 Chromatic Carapace. 10 Brilliant Chromatic Scales. 10 Blood of Heroes. 5 Skin of Shadow.",r={"Brilliant Chromatic Scale (10)","Blood of Heroes (10)","Skin of Shadow (5)"}},
[5168]={o="Bring Davil's Libram and Redpath's Shield to Carlin Redpath.",r={"Davil's Libram (1)","Redpath's Shield (1)"}},
[5181]={o="Bring the Skull of Horgus and the Shattered Sword of Marduk to Carlin Redpath at Light's Hope Chapel.",r={"Skull of Horgus (1)","Shattered Sword of Marduk (1)"}},
[5201]={o="Rivern Frostwind wants you to slay 5 Winterfall Shaman and 5 Winterfall Ursa.",r={"Winterfall Shaman (5)","Winterfall Ursa (5)"}},
[5202]={o="Search through Jaedenar to discover what the Blood Red Key is used for."},
[5203]={o="Escort Arko'narin to where Lightforge and her equipment are being held, and then protect her as you escape Shadow Hold. Afterwards, seek out Jessir Moonbow in Felwood to let her know what's happened to her friends.",r={"Protect Arko'narin out of Shadow Hold (1)"}},
[5204]={o="Return to Jaedenar and kill the succubus Rakaiah before finding the Remains of Trey Lightforge.",r={"Rakaiah (1)"}},
[5206]={o="Bring 5 Resonating Skulls and the Mystic Crystal to Carlin Redpath in Eastern Plaguelands.",r={"Resonating Skull (5)","Fetid Skull (99)"}},
[5210]={o="Bring the Extended Annals of Darrowshire to Carlin Redpath in Eastern Plaguelands."},
[5211]={o="Free 15 Darrowshire Spirits and return to Carlin Redpath.",r={"Darrowshire Spirits Freed (15)"}},
[5212]={o="Recover 20 Plagued Flesh Samples from Stratholme and return them to Betina Bigglezink. You suspect that any creature in Stratholme would have said flesh sample.",r={"Plagued Flesh Sample (20)"}},
[5213]={o="Travel to Stratholme and search the ziggurats. Find and return new Scourge Data to Betina Bigglezink.",r={"Scourge Data (1)"}},
[5214]={o="Find Fras Siabi's smoke shop in Stratholme and recover a box of Siabi's Premium Tobacco. Return to Smokey LaRue when the job is done.",r={"Grimm's Premium Tobacco (1)"}},
[5215]={o="Speak with High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Point, Western Plaguelands."},
[5216]={o="Go to Felstone Field in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there. &nbsp;It may have a key that will allow access to the cauldron. &nbsp;You must have the Empty Felstone Field Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.",r={"Felstone Field Cauldron Key (1)"}},
[5217]={o="Bring the Filled Felstone Field Bottle to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands."},
[5218]={o="The Scourge's plague cauldron stands before you, spewing vast amounts of toxins into the air. &nbsp;A small, non-descript access panel lies in the base of the cauldron's vast platform. Having already defeated the cauldron lord and acquired its key, you are free to add the appropriate reagents to the cauldron to make a counter agent to the plague.",r={"Arcane Quickener (1)","Osseous Agitator (6)","Runecloth (4)"}},
[5219]={o="Go to Dalson's Tears in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there, and use its key to gain access to the cauldron. &nbsp;You must have the Empty Dalson's Tears Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.",r={"Dalson's Tears Cauldron Key (1)"}},
[5220]={o="Bring the Filled Dalson's Tears Bottle to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands."},
[5221]={o="The Scourge's plague cauldron stands before you, spewing vast amounts of toxins into the air. &nbsp;A small, non-descript access panel lies in the base of the cauldron's vast platform. Having already defeated the cauldron lord and acquired its key, you are free to add the appropriate reagents to the cauldron to make a counter agent to the plague.",r={"Arcane Quickener (1)","Somatic Intensifier (5)","Runecloth (4)"}},
[5222]={o="Go to the Writhing Haunt in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there, and use its key to gain access to the cauldron. &nbsp;You must have the Empty Writhing Haunt Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.",r={"Writhing Haunt Cauldron Key (1)"}},
[5223]={o="Bring the Filled Writhing Haunt Bottle to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands."},
[5224]={o="The Scourge's plague cauldron stands before you, spewing vast amounts of toxins into the air. &nbsp;A small, non-descript access panel lies in the base of the cauldron's vast platform. Having already defeated the cauldron lord and acquired its key, you are free to add the appropriate reagents to the cauldron to make a counter agent to the plague.",r={"Arcane Quickener (1)","Somatic Intensifier (5)","Runecloth (4)"}},
[5225]={o="Go to Gahrron's Withering in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there, and use its key to gain access to the cauldron. &nbsp;You must have the Empty Gahrron's Withering Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.",r={"Gahrron's Withering Cauldron Key (1)"}},
[5226]={o="Bring the Filled Gahrron's Withering Bottle to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands."},
[5227]={o="The Scourge's plague cauldron stands before you, spewing vast amounts of toxins into the air. &nbsp;A small, non-descript access panel lies in the base of the cauldron's vast platform. Having already defeated the cauldron lord and acquired its key, you are free to add the appropriate reagents to the cauldron to make a counter agent to the plague.",r={"Arcane Quickener (1)","Ectoplasmic Resonator (4)","Runecloth (4)"}},
[5228]={o="Speak with Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands."},
[5229]={o="Go to Felstone Field in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there. &nbsp;It may have a key that will allow access to the cauldron. &nbsp;You must have the Empty Felstone Field Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.",r={"Felstone Field Cauldron Key (1)"}},
[5230]={o="Bring the Filled Felstone Field Bottle to Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands."},
[5231]={o="Go to Dalson's Tears in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there, and use its key to gain access to the cauldron. &nbsp;You must have the Empty Dalson's Tears Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.",r={"Dalson's Tears Cauldron Key (1)"}},
[5232]={o="Bring the Filled Dalson's Tears Bottle to Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands."},
[5233]={o="Go to the Writhing Haunt in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there, and use its key to gain access to the cauldron. &nbsp;You must have the Empty Writhing Haunt Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.",r={"Writhing Haunt Cauldron Key (1)"}},
[5234]={o="Bring the Filled Writhing Haunt Bottle to Shadow Priestess Vandis at The Bulwark, Western Plaguelands."},
[5235]={o="Go to Gahrron's Withering in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there, and use its key to gain access to the cauldron. &nbsp;You must have the Empty Gahrron's Withering Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.",r={"Gahrron's Withering Cauldron Key (1)"}},
[5236]={o="Bring the Filled Gahrron's Withering Bottle to Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands."},
[5237]={o="&lt;name&gt;, your successful re-engineering of the cauldrons is a tremendous victory for us! Let all within my presence hear: for service to the Kingdom of Stormwind and to the Alliance above and beyond the call of duty - in the face of overwhelming odds and incredible danger, might I add - I give &lt;name&gt; this, and I extend upon him our undying gratitude as a true hero of the Alliance. &nbsp;Cheers, I say!"},
[5238]={o="&lt;name&gt;, your successful re-engineering of the cauldrons is a tremendous victory for us! Let all within my presence hear: for service to the Forsaken and to the Horde as a whole above and beyond what was expected - in the face of overwhelming odds and incredible danger, might I add - I give &lt;name&gt; this, and I extend upon him our undying gratitude as a true hero of the Horde. &nbsp;Huzzah!"},
[5241]={o="Find Carlin Redpath."},
[5242]={o="Kill Moora and Salia, and bring Shadow Lord Fel'dan's Head to Greta Mosshoof in Felwood.",r={"Moora (1)","Salia (1)","Shadow Lord Fel'dan's Head (1)"}},
[5243]={o="Travel to Stratholme, in the north. Search the supply crates that litter the city and recover 5 Stratholme Holy Water. Return to Leonid Barthalomew the Revered when you have collected enough of the blessed fluid.",r={"Stratholme Holy Water (5)"}},
[5244]={o="Speak with Jaron Stoneshaper in Starfall Village."},
[5245]={o="Use Jaron's Pick to find the four Highborne Relic Fragments. Bring them to Aurora Skycaller in Eastern Plaguelands.",r={"First Relic Fragment (1)","Second Relic Fragment (1)","Third Relic Fragment (1)","Fourth Relic Fragment (1)"}},
[5246]={o="Find the Sacred Highborne Writings in the Temple of Zin-Malor in Azshara, and bring them to Aurora Skycaller near the Northpass Tower in Eastern Plaguelands.",r={"Sacred Highborne Writings (1)"}},
[5247]={o="Bring an Enchanted Thorium Bar, 5 Crystal Restore, and a Vial of Dire Water to Aurora Skycaller near the Northpass Tower in Eastern Plaguelands.",r={"Enchanted Thorium Bar (1)","Crystal Restore (5)","Vial of Dire Water (1)"}},
[5248]={o="Take the Crystal of Zin-Malor to Lake Kel'Theril in Winterspring and find a highborne spirit that will speak to you."},
[5249]={o="Find Starfall Village in Winterspring and speak with Wynd Nightchaser."},
[5250]={o="Find Starfall in Winterspring and speak with Wynd Nightchaser."},
[5251]={o="Travel to Stratholme and find Archivist Galford of the Scarlet Crusade. Destroy him and burn down the Scarlet Archive.",r={"Archivist Galford (1)","Archive Burned (1)"}},
[5252]={o="Speak with Wynd Nightchaser in Starfall Village, and ask about the proper place for the Crystal of Zin-Malor."},
[5253]={o="Deliver the Crystal of Zin-Malor to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus."},
[5261]={o="Speak with Eagan Peltskinner.",s="Deputy Willem",e="Eagan Peltskinner"},
[5262]={o="Take the Head of Balnazzar to Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff in the Eastern Plaguelands."},
[5263]={o="Venture to Stratholme and destroy Baron Rivendare. Take his head and return to Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff.",r={"Head of Baron Rivendare (1)"}},
[5264]={o="Speak with Lord Maxwell Tyrosus. He is inside the church."},
[5265]={o="Open the Argent Hold and claim your reward."},
[5281]={o="Find Egan. You only know that he was last seen around Stratholme."},
[5282]={o="Use Egan's Blaster on the ghostly and spectral citizens of Stratholme. When the restless souls break free from their ghostly shells, use the blaster again - freedom will be theirs! Free 15 Restless Souls and return to Egan.",r={"Souls Freed (15)"}},
[5283]={o="To become an Armorsmith, you must make the following items and return them to Grumnus: 4 Ornate Mithril Helms, 2 Ornate Mithril Boots, 1 Ornate Mithril Breastplate.",r={"Ornate Mithril Helm (4)","Ornate Mithril Boots (2)","Ornate Mithril Breastplate (1)"}},
[5284]={o="To become a Weaponsmith, you must make the following items and return them to Ironus: 4 Moonsteel Broadswords, 4 Massive Iron Axes, 2 Heavy Mithril Axes, and 2 Big Black Maces.",r={"Moonsteel Broadsword (4)","Massive Iron Axe (4)","Heavy Mithril Axe (2)","Big Black Mace (2)"}},
[5301]={o="To become an armorsmith, you must make the following items and return them to Okothos: 4 Ornate Mithril Helms, 2 Ornate Mithril Boots, 1 Ornate Mithril Breastplate.",r={"Ornate Mithril Helm (4)","Ornate Mithril Boots (2)","Ornate Mithril Breastplate (1)"}},
[5302]={o="To become a Weaponsmith, you must make the following items and return them to Borgosh: 4 Moonsteel Broadswords, 4 Massive Iron Axes, 2 Heavy Mithril Axes, and 2 Big Black Maces.",r={"Moonsteel Broadsword (4)","Massive Iron Axe (4)","Heavy Mithril Axe (2)","Big Black Mace (2)"}},
[5305]={o="Travel to Stratholme and kill the Crimson Hammersmith. Recover the Crimson Hammersmith's Apron and return to Lilith.",r={"Crimson Hammersmith's Apron (1)"}},
[5306]={o="Travel to Blackrock Spire and slay Shadow Hunter Vosh'gajin. Recover Vosh'gajin's Snakestone and return to Kilram.",r={"Vosh'gajin's Snakestone (1)"}},
[5307]={o="Find the Black Guard Swordsmith in Stratholme and destroy him. Recover the Insignia of the Black Guard and return to Seril Scourgebane.",r={"Insignia of the Black Guard (1)"}},
[5321]={o="Escort Kerlonian Evershade to Liladris Moonriver south along the road to find his bag in Darkshore.",r={"Horn of Awakening (1)","Kerlonian Evershade (1)","Escort Kerlonian Evershade on the road south to his bag (1)"},s="Kerlonian Evershade",e="Liladris Moonriver"},
[5341]={o="Venture to the Scholomance and recover the Barov family fortune. Four deeds make up this fortune: The Deed to Caer Darrow; The Deed to Brill; The Deed to Tarren Mill; and The Deed to Southshore. Return to Alexi Barov when you have completed this task.",r={"The Deed to Brill (1)","The Deed to Caer Darrow (1)","The Deed to Southshore (1)","The Deed to Tarren Mill (1)"}},
[5342]={o="Travel to Chillwind Camp - Alliance territory - and assassinate Weldon Barov. Take his head and return to Alexi Barov. Be warned, Weldon will probably be well protected by Alliance scum.",r={"Head of Weldon Barov (1)"}},
[5343]={o="Venture to the Scholomance and recover the Barov family fortune. Four deeds make up this fortune: The Deed to Caer Darrow; The Deed to Brill; The Deed to Tarren Mill; and The Deed to Southshore. Return to Weldon Barov when you have completed this task.",r={"The Deed to Brill (1)","The Deed to Caer Darrow (1)","The Deed to Southshore (1)","The Deed to Tarren Mill (1)"}},
[5344]={o="Travel to the Bulwark - Horde territory - and assassinate Alexi Barov. Take his head and return to Weldon Barov. Be warned, Alexi will probably be well protected by Horde filth.",r={"Head of Alexi Barov (1)"}},
[5361]={o="Deliver Cliffwatcher Longhorn Report to Nataka Longhorn at Ghost Walker Post in Desolace."},
[5381]={o="Retrieve the Demon Box from Thunder Axe Fortress, and return it, along with the Demon Pick to Taiga Wisemane in Shadowprey Village.",r={"Demon Box (1)"}},
[5382]={o="Find Doctor Theolen Krastinov inside the Scholomance. Destroy him, then burn the Remains of Eva Sarkhoff and the Remains of Lucien Sarkhoff. Return to Eva Sarkhoff when the task is complete.",r={"Doctor Theolen Krastinov (1)","Remains of Eva Sarkhoff Burned (1)","Remains of Lucien Sarkhoff Burned (1)"}},
[5384]={o="Return to the Scholomance with the Blood of Innocents. Find the porch and place the Blood of Innocents in the brazier. Kirtonos will come to feast upon your soul. Fight valiantly, do not give an inch! Destroy Kirtonos and return to Eva Sarkhoff.",r={"Kirtonos the Herald (1)"}},
[5385]={o="Return the Remains of Trey Lightforge to Jessir Moonbow in Felwood."},
[5386]={o="Talk to Jinar'Zillen at Shadowprey Village, and then bring Nataka Longhorn 2 Bloodbelly fish.",r={"Bloodbelly Fish (2)"}},
[5401]={o="All who fight evil on behalf of the Argent Dawn must don our commission. &nbsp;Wearing such will earn your right to claim rewards our quartermasters have to offer. While under commission, you'll be able to acquire Scourgestones from slain Scourge; these are marks of insignia that they sometimes possess. &nbsp;Procure these insignia and bring them to me. &nbsp;For each set you turn in, you will receive our marker of heroism - the Argent Dawn Valor Token. Achieve your destiny, &lt;class&gt; - join the fight today!"},
[5402]={o="A Minion's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge rank and file. &nbsp;These are sometimes found on the weaker of their troops positioned in the Plaguelands, though the term \"weaker\" is certainly to be considered in context. &nbsp;The Scourge, no matter where they are, should never be underestimated. The Argent Dawn currently offers a valor token in exchange for twenty of these insignia - an exchange I'm happy to do, provided you have earned enough scourgestones!",r={"Minion's Scourgestone (20)"}},
[5403]={o="An Invader's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge's elite troops. &nbsp;These are sometimes found on the stronger of the troops positioned in the Plaguelands. &nbsp;Slaying such a creature is indeed a challenge, but one that should be relished with a commission to vanquish evil. The Argent Dawn currently offers a valor token in exchange for ten of these insignia. &nbsp;Bring them to me here, and I will make sure you receive your just reward.",r={"Invader's Scourgestone (10)"}},
[5404]={o="A Corruptor's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge's overlords. &nbsp;A powerful being that holds a position of authority over the Scourge will always possess one. &nbsp;To slay such a malevolent creature would surely advance the cause of the Argent Dawn, and all good causes! On behalf of the Argent Dawn, I will give you a valor token in exchange for just a single one these insignia. &nbsp;Use caution in acquiring one, &lt;name&gt; - such powerful beings are not to be trifled with.",r={"Corruptor's Scourgestone (1)"}},
[5405]={o="All who fight evil on behalf of the Argent Dawn must don our commission. &nbsp;Wearing such will earn your right to claim rewards our quartermasters have to offer. While under commission, you'll be able to acquire Scourgestones from slain Scourge; these are marks of insignia that they sometimes possess. &nbsp;Procure these insignia and bring them to me. &nbsp;For each set you turn in, you will receive our marker of heroism - the Argent Dawn Valor Token. Achieve your destiny, &lt;class&gt; - join the fight today!"},
[5406]={o="A Corruptor's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge's overlords. &nbsp;A powerful being that holds a position of authority over the Scourge will always possess one. &nbsp;To slay such a malevolent creature would surely advance the cause of the Argent Dawn, and all good causes! On behalf of the Argent Dawn, I will give you a valor token in exchange for just a single one these insignia. &nbsp;Use caution in acquiring one, &lt;name&gt; - such powerful beings are not to be trifled with.",r={"Corruptor's Scourgestone (1)"}},
[5407]={o="An Invader's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge's elite troops. &nbsp;These are sometimes found on the stronger of the troops positioned in the Plaguelands. &nbsp;Slaying such a creature is indeed a challenge, but one that should be relished with a commission to vanquish evil. The Argent Dawn currently offers a valor token in exchange for ten of these insignia. &nbsp;Bring them to me here, and I will make sure you receive your just reward.",r={"Invader's Scourgestone (10)"}},
[5408]={o="A Minion's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge rank and file. &nbsp;These are sometimes found on the weaker of their troops positioned in the Plaguelands, though the term \"weaker\" is certainly to be considered in context. &nbsp;The Scourge, no matter where they are, should never be underestimated. The Argent Dawn currently offers a valor token in exchange for twenty of these insignia - an exchange I'm happy to do, provided you have earned enough scourgestones!",r={"Minion's Scourgestone (20)"}},
[5421]={o="I'll reward anyone who makes my life a bit easier... I enjoy doing as little as possible, mon! Below the docks here in Shadowprey Village, I've many shellfish traps. &nbsp;If you're kind enough to do my work and collect me my shellfish, then I'll reward you with something you want... get my drift mon? &nbsp;For every five shellfish you bring me I will give you a fine Bloodbelly fish!",r={"Shellfish (5)"}},
[5441]={o="Use the Foreman's Blackjack on Lazy Peons when they're sleeping. &nbsp;Wake up 5 peons, then return the Foreman's Blackjack to Foreman Thazz'ril in the Valley of Trials.",r={"Peons Awoken (5)"}},
[5461]={o="Travel to the Arathi Highlands, to the ruins of Stromgarde. Search Stromgarde for a Keepsake of Remembrance. If you find such an item, return with it to Magistrate Marduke.",r={"Keepsake of Remembrance (1)"}},
[5462]={o="Travel to Light's Hope in Eastern Plaguelands and seek out Leonid Barthalomew the Revered. Show him the Keepsake of Remembrance and tell him all that you have discovered."},
[5463]={o="Travel to Stratholme and find Menethil's Gift. Place the Keepsake of Remembrance upon the unholy ground."},
[5464]={o="Take the Soulbound Keepsake to Leonid Barthalomew in Eastern Plaguelands."},
[5465]={o="Return to Magistrate Marduke in Caer Darrow. Show him the Soulbound Keepsake."},
[5466]={o="Find Ras Frostwhisper in the Scholomance. When you have found him, use the Soulbound Keepsake on his undead visage. Should you succeed in reverting him to a mortal, strike him down and recover the Human Head of Ras Frostwhisper. Take the head back to Magistrate Marduke.",r={"Human Head of Ras Frostwhisper (1)"}},
[5481]={o="Collect 3 Gloom Weed and deliver them to Junior Apothecary Holland in the Brill graveyard.",r={"Gloom Weed (3)"}},
[5482]={o="Collect 10 Doom Weed and deliver them back to Junior Apothecary Holland.",r={"Doom Weed (10)"}},
[5501]={o="Bring 10 Kodo Bones from the Kodo Graveyard to Bibbly F'utzbuckle at Kormek's Hut.",r={"Kodo Bone (10)"}},
[5503]={o="All who fight evil on behalf of the Argent Dawn must don our commission. &nbsp;Wearing such will earn your right to claim rewards our quartermasters have to offer. While under commission, you'll be able to acquire Scourgestones from slain Scourge; these are marks of insignia that they sometimes possess. &nbsp;Procure these insignia and bring them to me. &nbsp;For each set you turn in, you will receive our marker of heroism - the Argent Dawn Valor Token. Achieve your destiny, &lt;class&gt; - join the fight today!"},
[5504]={o="Bring 10 Argent Dawn Valor Tokens to Quartermaster Hasana at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Argent Dawn Valor Token (10)","Argent Dawn: (1)"}},
[5505]={o="Well, here you are &lt;name&gt; - the completed Skeleton Key. &nbsp;I am certain as I can be that this key will allow you within the confines of the Scholomance. &nbsp;There's only one way to be absolutely sure it works, though. &nbsp;Waste no time in trying it out, I say. Good luck, mighty hero. &nbsp;May you continue to bring light unto the darkness!"},
[5507]={o="Bring 10 Argent Dawn Valor Tokens to Quartermaster Lightspark at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Argent Dawn Valor Token (10)","Argent Dawn: (1)"}},
[5508]={o="A Corruptor's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge's overlords. &nbsp;A powerful being that holds a position of authority over the Scourge will always possess one. &nbsp;To slay such a malevolent creature would surely advance the cause of the Argent Dawn, and all good causes! On behalf of the Argent Dawn, I will give you a valor token in exchange for just a single one of these insignia. &nbsp;Use caution in acquiring one, &lt;name&gt; - such powerful beings are not to be trifled with.",r={"Corruptor's Scourgestone (1)"}},
[5509]={o="An Invader's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge's elite troops. &nbsp;These are sometimes found on the stronger of the troops positioned in the Plaguelands. &nbsp;Slaying such a creature is indeed a challenge, but one that should be relished with a commission to vanquish evil. The Argent Dawn currently offers a valor token in exchange for ten of these insignia. &nbsp;Bring them to me here, and I will make sure you receive your just reward.",r={"Invader's Scourgestone (10)"}},
[5510]={o="A Minion's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge rank and file. &nbsp;These are sometimes found on the weaker of their troops positioned in the Plaguelands, though the term \"weaker\" is certainly to be considered in context. &nbsp;The Scourge, no matter where they are, should never be underestimated. The Argent Dawn currently offers a valor token in exchange for twenty of these insignia - an exchange I'm happy to do, provided you have earned enough scourgestones!",r={"Minion's Scourgestone (20)"}},
[5511]={o="Well, here you are &lt;name&gt; - the completed Skeleton Key. &nbsp;I am certain as I can be that this key will allow you within the confines of the Scholomance. &nbsp;There's only one way to be absolutely sure it works, though. &nbsp;Waste no time in trying it out, I say. Good luck, mighty hero. &nbsp;May your victories continue to bring you fame and power as you lay waste to Scholomance!"},
[5513]={o="Bring 10 Argent Dawn Valor Tokens to Quartermaster Breechlock at Light's Hope Chapel, Eastern Plaguelands.",r={"Argent Dawn Valor Token (10)","Argent Dawn: (1)"}},
[5514]={o="Bring the Imbued Skeletal Fragments and 15 gold coins to Krinkle Goodsteel in Gadgetzan.",r={"Money: 15 &nbsp; (1)"}},
[5515]={o="Locate Jandice Barov in the Scholomance and destroy her. From her corpse recover Krastinov's Bag of Horrors. Return the bag to Eva Sarkhoff.",r={"Krastinov's Bag of Horrors (1)"}},
[5517]={o="Bring 25 Argent Dawn Valor Tokens to Quartermaster Breechlock at Light's Hope Chapel, Eastern Plaguelands.",r={"Argent Dawn Valor Token (25)","Argent Dawn: (1)"}},
[5518]={o="Bring 4 Bolts of Runecloth, 8 Rugged Leather, 2 Rune Threads, and Ogre Tannin to Knot Thimblejack. &nbsp;He is currently chained inside the Gordok wing of Dire Maul.",r={"Bolt of Runecloth (4)","Rugged Leather (8)","Rune Thread (2)","Ogre Tannin (1)"}},
[5519]={o="Need another suit, do ya? &nbsp;Well, I'm not going anywhere soon it seems - bring me the same things I asked for from before, and I'll make you another ogre suit.",r={"Bolt of Runecloth (4)","Rugged Leather (8)","Rune Thread (2)","Ogre Tannin (1)"}},
[5521]={o="Bring 25 Argent Dawn Valor Tokens to Quartermaster Lightspark at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Argent Dawn Valor Token (25)","Argent Dawn: (1)"}},
[5522]={o="Bring the Frozen Eggs to Leonid Barthalomew in the Eastern Plaguelands."},
[5524]={o="Bring 25 Argent Dawn Valor Tokens to Quartermaster Hasana at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Argent Dawn Valor Token (25)","Argent Dawn: (1)"}},
[5525]={o="It's called the Gordok Shackle Key - well, that's what these \"tons o' fun\" keep calling it. &nbsp;I think any of the ogres might have it, but I'm not sure if any specific ones do. &nbsp;Maybe the guards have a better chance of having one... What am I talking about - you have it already, don't you?! &nbsp;Is that it there??!",r={"Gordok Shackle Key (1)"}},
[5526]={o="Find the Felvine in Dire Maul and acquire a shard from it. &nbsp;Chances are you'll only be able to procure one with the demise of Alzzin the Wildshaper. &nbsp;Use the Reliquary of Purity to securely seal the shard inside, and return it to Rabine Saturna in Nighthaven, Moonglade.",r={"Sealed Reliquary of Purity (1)","Felvine Shard (1)"}},
[5527]={o="Travel to Silithus and search for a Reliquary of Purity within the ruins of Southwind Village. &nbsp;If you are able to find it, return with it to Rabine Saturna in Nighthaven, Moonglade.",r={"Reliquary of Purity (1)"}},
[5528]={o="You da big boss now, so you get free sample of my better brews! &nbsp;These drinks boost you up AND give you good buzz! &nbsp;These are da good ones, chief... you try and tell Kreeg yourself!"},
[5529]={o="Kill 20 Plagued Hatchlings, then return to Betina Bigglezink at the Light's Hope Chapel.",r={"Plagued Hatchling (20)"}},
[5531]={o="Bring the Frozen Eggs to Betina Bigglezink."},
[5533]={o="Speak with Alchemist Arbington at Chillwind Point, Western Plaguelands."},
[5534]={o="Find Some Rune that the naga have in their possession in the Ruins of Eldarath and return it to Kim'jael in Azshara.",r={"Some Rune (1)"}},
[5535]={o="Destroy 6 Highborne Apparitions and 6 Highborne Lichlings before returning to Loh'atu in Azshara.",r={"Highborne Apparition (6)","Highborne Lichling (6)"}},
[5536]={o="Kill 6 Haldarr Satyr, 2 Haldarr Tricksters, 2 Haldarr Felsworn and then return to Loh'atu on the border of Ashenvale.",r={"Haldarr Satyr (6)","Haldarr Trickster (2)","Haldarr Felsworn (2)"}},
[5537]={o="Bring 15 Skeletal Fragments to Alchemist Arbington at Chillwind Point, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Skeletal Fragments (15)"}},
[5538]={o="Bring the Imbued Skeletal Fragments and 15 gold coins to Krinkle Goodsteel in Gadgetzan.",r={"Money: 15 &nbsp; (1)"}},
[5541]={o="Bring Rumbleshot's Ammo to Hegnar Rumbleshot in Dun Morogh.",r={"Rumbleshot's Ammo (1)"},s="Loslor Rudge",e="Hegnar Rumbleshot"},
[5542]={o="Slay 20 Plaguehound Runts, 5 Plaguehounds and 5 Frenzied Plaguehounds. Return to Tirion Fordring when the task is complete.",r={"Plaguehound Runt (20)","Plaguehound (5)","Frenzied Plaguehound (5)"}},
[5543]={o="Slay 30 Plaguebats and return to Tirion Fordring.",r={"Plaguebat (30)"}},
[5544]={o="Seek out the Carrion Grubs and Devourers of the region. Slay them and harvest their meat. Return to Tirion Fordring when you have gathered 15 Slabs of Carrion Worm Meat.",r={"Slab of Carrion Worm Meat (15)"}},
[5545]={o="Bring 8 Bundles of Wood to Raelen at the Eastvale Logging Camp.",r={"Bundle of Wood (8)"},s="Supervisor Raelen",e="Supervisor Raelen"},
[5561]={o="Bring five Tamed Kodos and the Kodo Kombobulator back to Smeed Scrabblescrew at Scrabblescrew's Camp.",r={"Kodos Tamed (5)"}},
[5581]={o="Banish 6 Portals at Mannoroc Coven and return to Taiga Wisemane at Shadowprey Village.",r={"Portals Banished (6)"}},
[5582]={o="Bring the Healthy Dragon Scale to Betina Bigglezink at the Light's Hope Chapel in Eastern Plaguelands."},
[5601]={o="Find Pamela Redpath in Darrowshire."},
[5621]={o="Find Sentinel Shaya and heal her wounds using Lesser Heal (Rank 2). Afterwards, grant her Power Word: Fortitude and then return to Laurna Morninglight in Dolanaar.",r={"Heal and fortify Sentinel Shaya (1)"},s="Laurna Morninglight",e="Laurna Morninglight"},
[5622]={o="Speak to Laurna Morninglight in Teldrassil.",s="Shanda",e="Laurna Morninglight"},
[5623]={o="Speak to Priestess Josetta in Elwynn Forest.",s="Priestess Anetta",e="Priestess Josetta"},
[5624]={o="Find Guard Roberts and heal his wounds using Lesser Heal (Rank 2). Afterwards, grant him Power Word: Fortitude and then return to Priestess Josetta in Goldshire.",r={"Heal and fortify Guard Roberts (1)"},s="Priestess Josetta",e="Priestess Josetta"},
[5625]={o="Find Mountaineer Dolf and heal his wounds using Lesser Heal (Rank 2). Afterwards, grant him Power Word: Fortitude and then return to Maxan Anvol in Kharanos.",r={"Heal and fortify Mountaineer Dolf (1)"},s="Maxan Anvol",e="Maxan Anvol"},
[5626]={o="Speak to Maxan Anvol in Dun Morogh.",s="Branstock Khalder",e="Maxan Anvol"},
[5627]={o="You've proven yourself worthy of Elune's attention, &lt;name&gt;. If you feel you're ready, I would very much like to teach you one of her spells unique to our people.",s="Priestess Alathea",e="Priestess Alathea"},
[5628]={o="Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.",s="Priestess Josetta",e="Priestess Alathea"},
[5629]={o="Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.",s="Laurna Morninglight",e="Priestess Alathea"},
[5630]={o="Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.",s="Maxan Anvol",e="Priestess Alathea"},
[5631]={o="Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.",s="Brother Joshua",e="Priestess Alathea"},
[5632]={o="Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.",s="Nara Meideros"},
[5633]={o="Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.",s="Braenna Flintcrag",e="Priestess Alathea"},
[5634]={o="Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.",e="High Priestess Laurena"},
[5635]={o="Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.",s="Priestess Josetta",e="High Priestess Laurena"},
[5636]={o="Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.",s="Laurna Morninglight",e="High Priestess Laurena"},
[5637]={o="Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.",s="Maxan Anvol",e="High Priestess Laurena"},
[5638]={o="Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.",s="Nara Meideros",e="High Priestess Laurena"},
[5639]={o="I'm glad you've arrived, &lt;name&gt;. There are many things we will have to discuss, but more importantly is your training in the ways of the Light. There are lessons all servants of the Light must learn. If you are ready, we'll begin discussing some of those now.",s="High Priest Rohan",e="High Priestess Laurena"},
[5640]={o="Speak to High Priest Rohan in Stormwind.",s="Priestess Alathea",e="High Priestess Laurena"},
[5641]={o="You've got the makings of a great &lt;class&gt;, &lt;name&gt;. Keep up the good work! You've already shown you're ready for battle. Perhaps it's time we taught ya a little somethin' more.",s="High Priest Rohan",e="High Priest Rohan"},
[5642]={o="Speak to Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar."},
[5643]={o="Speak to Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar."},
[5644]={o="Speak to Aelthalyste in the Undercity."},
[5645]={o="Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.",s="High Priestess Laurena",e="High Priest Rohan"},
[5646]={o="Speak to Aelthalyste in the Undercity."},
[5647]={o="Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.",s="Priestess Alathea",e="High Priest Rohan"},
[5648]={o="Find Grunt Kor'ja and heal her wounds using Lesser Heal (Rank 2). Afterwards, grant her Power Word: Fortitude and then return to Tai'jin at Razor Hill.",r={"Heal and fortify Grunt Kor'ja (1)"}},
[5649]={o="Speak to Tai'jin in Durotar."},
[5650]={o="Find Deathguard Kel and heal his wounds using Lesser Heal (Rank 2). Afterwards, grant him Power Word: Fortitude and then return to Dark Cleric Beryl in Brill.",r={"Heal and fortify Deathguard Kel (1)"}},
[5651]={o="Speak to Dark Cleric Beryl in Tirisfal Glades."},
[5652]={o="You would do well to pay heed to this lesson, young one. The Hex of Weakness will be a great boon to you in battle. Later I will have tests for you to further yourself and prove your worth to the tribe."},
[5654]={o="Speak to Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar."},
[5655]={o="Speak to Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar."},
[5656]={o="Speak to Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar."},
[5657]={o="Speak to Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar."},
[5658]={o="Ah, young &lt;class&gt;, I am glad you have returned here. I would teach you a lesson you would do well to not forget. Are you prepared?"},
[5660]={o="Speak to Aelthalyste in the Undercity."},
[5661]={o="Speak to Aelthalyste in the Undercity."},
[5662]={o="Speak to Aelthalyste in the Undercity."},
[5663]={o="Speak to Aelthalyste in the Undercity."},
[5672]={o="By devoting yourself to Elune and our people, you have attained a state that not all of us can achieve. It is tradition that you then be taught even greater abilities for your devotion. Do you accept?",s="Priestess Alathea",e="Priestess Alathea"},
[5673]={o="Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.",s="High Priestess Laurena",e="Priestess Alathea"},
[5674]={o="Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.",s="Nara Meideros",e="Priestess Alathea"},
[5675]={o="Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.",s="High Priest Rohan",e="Priestess Alathea"},
[5676]={o="We were forced to learn some magics to protect us from what is commonly called our greatest enemy: the arcane. I would teach you a spell to help you defend yourself and your companions from those who would wield such power.",s="High Priestess Laurena",e="High Priestess Laurena"},
[5677]={o="Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.",s="High Priest Rohan",e="High Priestess Laurena"},
[5678]={o="Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.",s="Priestess Alathea",e="High Priestess Laurena"},
[5679]={o="I would teach you Devouring Plague if you feel you are prepared, &lt;name&gt;. A spell of no small power, it will aid you in your coming battles. Practice with it--there will be tests later."},
[5680]={o="Your rites will come soon enough. For now, I teach you a spell that will be of great use to you when you do battle with your enemies."},
[5713]={o="Protect Sentinel Aynasha, then speak with Onaeya at Maestra's Post in Ashenvale.",r={"Protect Aynasha (1)"},s="Sentinel Aynasha",e="Sentinel Onaeya"},
[5721]={o="Place the Relic Bundle at the Darrowshire town square. Prevent Davil Lightfire's death until the death of Horgus. Prevent Captain Redpath's death until Redpath the Corrupted appears. Defeat Redpath the Corrupted. Speak with the spirit of Joseph Redpath when he appears at the town square, then speak with Pamela at her home.",r={"Accept Redpath's Forgiveness (1)"}},
[5722]={o="Search Ragefire Chasm for Maur Grimtotem's corpse and search it for any items of interest.",s="Rahauro",e="Maur Grimtotem"},
[5723]={o="Search Orgrimmar for Ragefire Chasm, then kill 8 Ragefire Troggs and 8 Ragefire Shaman before returning to Rahauro in Thunder Bluff.",r={"Ragefire Trogg slain (8)","Ragefire Shaman slain (8)"},s="Rahauro",e="Rahauro"},
[5724]={o="Take the Grimtotem Satchel to Rahauro in Thunder Bluff.",r={"Grimtotem Satchel (Provided) (1)"},s="Maur Grimtotem",e="Rahauro"},
[5725]={o="Bring the books Spells of Shadow and Incantations from the Nether to Varimathras in Undercity.",r={"Spells of Shadow (1)","Incantations from the Nether (1)"},s="Varimathras",e="Varimathras"},
[5726]={o="Bring a Lieutenant's Insignia to Thrall in Orgrimmar.",r={"Lieutenant's Insignia (1)"},s="Thrall",e="Thrall"},
[5727]={o="Take the Lieutenant's Insignia to Neeru Fireblade and speak to him. Gauge if he believes you are a member of the Burning Blade and then return to Thrall in Orgrimmar.",r={"Gauge Neeru Fireblade's reaction to you being a member of the Burning Blade (1)"},s="Thrall",e="Thrall"},
[5728]={o="Kill Bazzalan and Jergosh the Invoker before returning to Thrall in Orgrimmar.",r={"Bazzalan slain (1)","Jergosh the Invoker slain (1)"},s="Thrall",e="Thrall"},
[5729]={o="Speak to Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar.",s="Thrall",e="Neeru Fireblade"},
[5730]={o="Speak to Thrall in Orgrimmar and tell him what you've learned.",s="Neeru Fireblade",e="Thrall"},
[5741]={o="Get the Sceptre of Light and then return it to Azore Aldamort at the tower in Ethel Rethor.",r={"Sceptre of Light (1)"}},
[5742]={o="Listen to what Tirion Fordring has to say.",r={"Tirion's Tale (1)"}},
[5761]={o="Enter Ragefire Chasm and slay Taragaman the Hungerer, then bring his heart back to Neeru Fireblade in Orgrimmar.",r={"Taragaman the Hungerer's Heart (1)"},s="Neeru Fireblade",e="Neeru Fireblade"},
[5762]={o="Take Kravel's Crate to Hemet Nesingwary in Stranglethorn.",s="Kravel Koalbeard",e="Hemet Nesingwary"},
[5763]={o="Bring Roon's Kodo Horn to Hemet Nesingwary in Stranglethorn."},
[5781]={o="Travel to the Undercroft - at the southernmost section of the Eastern Plaguelands - and recover Taelan's Hammer. Return to Tirion Fordring upon completion of your objective.",r={"Taelan's Hammer (1)"}},
[5801]={o="Take the Skeleton Key Mold and 2 Thorium Bars to the top of Fire Plume Ridge in Un'Goro Crater. &nbsp;Use the Skeleton Key Mold by the lava lake to forge the Unfinished Skeleton Key. Bring the Unfinished Skeleton Key to Alchemist Arbington at Chillwind Point, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Unfinished Skeleton Key (1)"}},
[5802]={o="Take the Skeleton Key Mold and 2 Thorium Bars to the top of Fire Plume Ridge in Un'Goro Crater. &nbsp;Use the Skeleton Key Mold by the lava lake to forge the Unfinished Skeleton Key. Bring the Unfinished Skeleton Key to Apothecary Dithers at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Unfinished Skeleton Key (1)"}},
[5803]={o="Destroy Araj the Summoner and bring Araj's Scarab to Alchemist Arbington at Chillwind Point, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Araj's Scarab (1)"}},
[5804]={o="Destroy Araj the Summoner and bring Araj's Scarab to Apothecary Dithers at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.",r={"Araj's Scarab (1)"}},
[5805]={o="Bring the Northshire Gift Voucher to Merissa Stilwell.",e="Merissa Stilwell"},
[5821]={o="Escort the Gizelton Caravan past the Kolkar Centaur village. Talk with Smeed at Scrabblescrew's Camp for your reward.",r={"Escort Gizelton Caravan past Kolkar Centaur Village (1)"}},
[5841]={o="Bring the Coldridge Valley Gift Voucher to Yori Crackhelm.",e="Yori Crackhelm"},
[5842]={o="Bring the Shadowglen Gift Voucher to Orenthil Whisperwind.",e="Orenthil Whisperwind"},
[5843]={o="Bring the Valley of Trials Gift Voucher to Magga."},
[5844]={o="Bring the Camp Narache Gift Voucher to Vorn Skyseer."},
[5845]={o="Travel to Northdale, in the northeastern region of the Eastern Plaguelands, and recover the Symbol of Lost Honor. Return to Tirion Fordring upon completion of your objective.",r={"Symbol of Lost Honor (1)"}},
[5846]={o="Travel to island of Caer Darrow, in the south-central region of the Plaguelands, and look for any clues as to the whereabouts of the painting."},
[5847]={o="Bring the Deathknell Gift Voucher to Claire Willower in Deathknell."},
[5848]={o="Travel to Stratholme, in the northern part of the Plaguelands. It is in the Scarlet Bastion that you will find the painting 'Of Love and Family,' hidden behind another painting depicting the twin moons of our world. Return the painting to Tirion Fordring.",r={"Of Love and Family (1)"}},
[5861]={o="Travel to Uther's Tomb, located in the southern Plaguelands. Show Myranda the Hag Tirion's Gift."},
[5862]={o="Speak to Myranda to gain the Scarlet Illusion. Travel to Hearthglen while under the Scarlet Illusion and deliver Tirion's Gift to Highlord Taelan Fordring. Hearthglen is to the north, Taelan should be inside of Mardenholde Keep."},
[5863]={o="Andi Lynn in Gadgetzan wants you to destroy the Dunemaul Compound by killing 10 Dunemaul Brutes, 10 Dunemaul Enforcers, and Gor'marok the Ravager.",r={"Dunemaul Brute (10)","Dunemaul Enforcer (10)","Gor'marok the Ravager (1)"}},
[5881]={o="Maggran wishes you to deliver a letter to Grish Longrunner at the Great Lift in the Barrens."},
[5882]={o="Possessing a Cenarion beacon allows one to see a corrupted soul shard on those tainted beasts that are put down for the greater good. &nbsp;I grind shards into a usable reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. &nbsp;We will use that salve to turn corrupted plants into healthy ones again. In exchange for these shards, I will give you some Cenarion plant salves I have already prepared.",r={"Corrupted Soul Shard (6)"}},
[5883]={o="If you possess a Cenarion beacon while mining in Felwood, you will be able to see tainted vitriol that corrupts a vein of raw metal. &nbsp;I know how to purify that vitriol and turn it into a reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. &nbsp;You will then use that salve on plants you find in the wild that need saving. If you have collected any tainted vitriol, I'll give you some Cenarion plant salve I have already prepared.",r={"Tainted Vitriol (4)"}},
[5884]={o="A Cenarion beacon allows a seasoned herbalist to spot insidious fel creep - a malfeasant product of Felwood's corruption. &nbsp;My work here has taught me the knowledge of purifying fel creep into a cleansing reagent... used in what we now refer to as Cenarion plant salve. When you gather herbs in Felwood, you should encounter the fel creep so long as you have the beacon. &nbsp;In exchange for what you bring to me, I will give you pre-made Cenarion plant salve.",r={"Fel Creep (4)"}},
[5885]={o="A Cenarion beacon will allow a well-trained skinner to spot patches of tainted skin from bounty gathered in Felwood. &nbsp;I convert these seemingly useless patches into a thick paste that serves as a quickening agent for Cenarion plant salve. &nbsp;When you skin your kills here in Felwood, be sure to have a beacon on you! When you collect tainted patches, bring them to me and I will give you some Cenarion plant salves that I have already made.",r={"Patch of Tainted Skin (5)"}},
[5886]={o="The power of a disenchanted magical item is felt by the essence it creates. &nbsp;I've devised a way to turn raw essence used by enchanters into a suitable reagent for creating Cenarion plant salve. &nbsp;You don't need a Cenarion beacon for this; any suitably disenchanted item that yields lesser nether essences will work. I just need a single lesser nether essence; in exchange, I will give you Cenarion plant salves. &nbsp;The essence is extremely potent - a little definitely goes a long way!",r={"Lesser Nether Essence (1)"}},
[5887]={o="Possessing a Cenarion beacon allows one to see a corrupted soul shard on those tainted beasts that are put down for the greater good. &nbsp;I grind shards into a usable reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. &nbsp;We will use that salve to turn corrupted plants into healthy ones again. In exchange for these shards, I will give you some Cenarion plant salves I have already prepared.",r={"Corrupted Soul Shard (6)"}},
[5888]={o="If you possess a Cenarion beacon while mining in Felwood, you will be able to see tainted vitriol that corrupts a vein of raw metal. &nbsp;I know how to purify that vitriol and turn it into a reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. &nbsp;You will then use that salve on plants you find in the wild that need saving. If you have collected any tainted vitriol, I'll give you some Cenarion plant salve I have already prepared.",r={"Tainted Vitriol (4)"}},
[5889]={o="A Cenarion beacon allows a seasoned herbalist to spot insidious fel creep - a malfeasant product of Felwood's corruption. &nbsp;My work here has taught me the knowledge of purifying fel creep into a cleansing reagent... used in what we now refer to as Cenarion plant salve. When you gather herbs in Felwood, you should encounter the fel creep so long as you have the beacon. &nbsp;In exchange for what you bring to me, I will give you pre-made Cenarion plant salve.",r={"Fel Creep (4)"}},
[5890]={o="A Cenarion beacon will allow a well-trained skinner to spot patches of tainted skin from bounty gathered in Felwood. &nbsp;I convert these seemingly useless patches into a thick paste that serves as a quickening agent for Cenarion plant salve. &nbsp;When you skin your kills here in Felwood, be sure to have a beacon on you! When you collect tainted patches, bring them to me and I will give you some Cenarion plant salves that I have already made.",r={"Patch of Tainted Skin (5)"}},
[5891]={o="The power of a disenchanted magical item is felt by the essence it creates. &nbsp;I've devised a way to turn raw essence used by enchanters into a suitable reagent for creating Cenarion plant salve. &nbsp;You don't need a Cenarion beacon for this; any suitably disenchanted item that yields lesser nether essences will work. I just need a single lesser nether essence; in exchange, I will give you Cenarion plant salves. &nbsp;The essence is extremely potent - a little definitely goes a long way!",r={"Lesser Nether Essence (1)"}},
[5901]={o="Use the Empty Termite Jar on the Termite Mounds in Eastern Plaguelands. After you've gathered 100 Plagueland Termites, return to Mickey Levine at the Bulwark in Tirisfal Glades.",r={"Plagueland Termites (100)"}},
[5902]={o="Find someplace suitable in the center of the Northridge Lumber Mill in Western Plaguelands to place the Barrel of Plagueland Termites."},
[5903]={o="Use the Empty Termite Jar on the Termite Mounds in Eastern Plaguelands. After you've gathered 100 Plagueland Termites, return to Nathaniel Dumah at Chillwind Camp in Western Plaguelands.",r={"Plagueland Termites (100)"}},
[5904]={o="Find someplace suitable in the center of the Northridge Lumber Mill in Western Plaguelands to place the Barrel of Plagueland Termites."},
[5921]={o="Use the spell \"Teleport: Moonglade\" to travel to Moonglade. &nbsp;When you arrive, speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven.",s="Mathrengyl Bearwalker",e="Dendrite Starblaze"},
[5922]={o="Use the spell \"Teleport: Moonglade\" to travel to Moonglade. &nbsp;When you arrive, speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven."},
[5923]={o="Speak with Mathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Enclave, Darnassus.",s="Denatharion",e="Mathrengyl Bearwalker"},
[5924]={o="Speak with Mathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Enclave, Darnassus.",s="Theridran",e="Mathrengyl Bearwalker"},
[5925]={o="Speak with Mathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Enclave, Darnassus.",s="Kal",e="Mathrengyl Bearwalker"},
