[6121]={o="Travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven.",s="Alfina Nightgaze",e="Dendrite Starblaze"},
[6122]={o="Use the Empty Cliffspring Falls Sampler to draw a sample of water from the mouth of the cave by the falls. Deliver the Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler to Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine, Darkshore.",r={"Filled Cliffspring Falls Sampler (1)"},s="Dendrite Starblaze",e="Alanndarian Nightsong"},
[6123]={o="Bring 5 Earthroot and 12 Lunar Funguses to Alanndarian Nightsong in Auberdine so she may make a curative salve.",r={"Earthroot (5)","Lunar Fungus (12)"},s="Alanndarian Nightsong",e="Alanndarian Nightsong"},
[6124]={o="Use the Curative Animal Salve on 10 Sickly Deer that are located throughout Darkshore; doing so should cure them. &nbsp;Sickly Deer have been reported starting south of the Cliffspring River to the north of Auberdine and extending all the way into southern Darkshore where the edge of Ashenvale begins.",r={"Sickly Deer cured (10)"},s="Alanndarian Nightsong",e="Dendrite Starblaze"},
[6125]={o="Return to Mathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Enclave, Darnassus.",s="Dendrite Starblaze",e="Mathrengyl Bearwalker"},
[6126]={o="Travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven."},
[6127]={o="Use the Empty Dreadmist Peak Sampler to draw a sample of water from a pool at the top of the peak. Deliver the Filled Dreadmist Peak Sampler to Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads, Barrens.",r={"Filled Dreadmist Peak Sampler (1)"}},
[6128]={o="Bring 5 Earthroot and 5 Kodo Horns to Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads so he may make a curative salve.",r={"Earthroot (5)","Kodo Horn (5)"}},
[6129]={o="Use the Curative Animal Salve on 10 Sickly Gazelles that are located throughout the northern part of the Barrens; doing so should cure them. &nbsp;Sickly Gazelles have been reported north of the east-west road that runs through the Crossroads.",r={"Sickly Gazelle cured (10)"}},
[6130]={o="Return to Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise, Thunder Bluff."},
[6131]={o="Grazle wants you to prove yourself by killing 5 Deadwood Warriors, 5 Deadwood Pathfinders, and 5 Deadwood Gardeners.",r={"Deadwood Warrior (5)","Deadwood Pathfinder (5)","Deadwood Gardener (5)"}},
[6132]={o="Escort Melizza Brimbuzzle, then speak with Hornizz Brimbuzzle at the Kodo Graveyard in Desolace."},
[6133]={o="Travel to the northern borders of the Eastern Plaguelands and recover the Quel'Thalas Registry. The item is somewhere in the Quel'Lithien lodge. You must also slay 8 Rangers, 8 Pathstriders, and 8 Woodsmen.",r={"Pathstrider (8)","Ranger (8)","Woodsman (8)","Quel'Thalas Registry (1)"}},
[6134]={o="Bring 8 Ghost-o-plasms and the Crate of Ghost Magnets to Hornizz Brimbuzzle in Desolace.",r={"Ghost-o-plasm (8)"}},
[6135]={o="Find Duskwing and slay him. From the corpse, recover a Patch of Duskwing's Fur and return it to Nathanos Blightcaller. It is said that Duskwing roams the countryside to the north of Marris Stead.",r={"Patch of Duskwing's Fur (1)"}},
[6136]={o="Find Borelgore in the northern wastes of Eastern Plaguelands and destroy him. Return to Nathanos Blightcaller when the mission is complete.",r={"Borelgore (1)"}},
[6141]={o="Speak with Brother Anton in Desolace."},
[6142]={o="Find 10 pieces of Soft-shelled Clam Meat and bring it back to Mai'Lahii at Shadowprey Village.",r={"Soft-shelled Clam Meat (10)","Soft-shelled Clam (10)"}},
[6143]={o="Slay 7 Slitherblade Myrmidon, 7 Slitherblade Naga, and 5 Slitherblade Sorceresses, and then talk to Drulzegar at Shadowprey in Desolace.",r={"Slitherblade Myrmidon (7)","Slitherblade Naga (7)","Slitherblade Sorceress (5)"}},
[6144]={o="Travel to the Undercity and speak with Varimathras."},
[6145]={o="Return to Eastern Plaguelands and track down the Crimson Courier. Kill the Courier and recover the Grand Crusader's Command. Take the command to Nathanos Blightcaller for further instruction.",r={"The Grand Crusader's Command (1)"}},
[6146]={o="Travel to Tyr's Hand, southeast of the Marris Stead. Once there, take a bite of the Rotten Apple. While under the guise of the Scarlet Crusade, deliver the Grand Crusader's Command to Crusader Lord Valdelmar.",r={"The Grand Crusader's Command (1)","Rotten Apple (1)"}},
[6147]={o="Return to Nathanos Blightcaller with the new information."},
[6148]={o="The Scarlet Crusade is on the move. Somewhere along the road from Tyr's Hand to Stratholme you will find the Oracle, Demetria, and her entourage. Hunt her down and slay her. Return to Nathanos Blightcaller should you succeed.",r={"Demetria (1)"}},
[6161]={o="Find Rackmore's Silver Key. &nbsp;Find Rackmore's Golden Key. &nbsp;Find and open Rackmore's Chest.",r={"Rackmore's Silver Key (1)","Rackmore's Golden Key (1)"}},
[6162]={o="Kill Overlord Ror and return his claw to Dreka'Sur at Bloodvenom Post in Felwood.",r={"Overlord Ror's Claw (1)"}},
[6163]={o="Travel to Stratholme and slay Ramstein the Gorger. Take his head as a souvenir for Nathanos.",r={"Head of Ramstein the Gorger (1)"}},
[6164]={o="Bring Augustus' Receipt Book to Augustus the Touched in Terrordale.",r={"Augustus' Receipt Book (1)"}},
[6181]={o="Bring Lewis' Note to Thor the gryphon master.",s="Quartermaster Lewis",e="Thor"},
[6182]={o="Speak with Mathias Shaw in Old Town Stormwind. He resides in the Barracks."},
[6183]={o="Speak with Mathias Shaw again if you wish to accept his task."},
[6184]={o="Travel to Chillwind Camp in the Western Plaguelands and meet up with your contact, Flint Shadowmore."},
[6185]={o="Scour the Eastern Plaguelands for clues as to the \"Blightcaller\" and the missing SI:7 agents. If you find any SI:7 Insignias, return them to Flint Shadowmore at Chillwind Camp.",r={"SI:7 Insignia (Rutger) (1)","SI:7 Insignia (Fredo) (1)","SI:7 Insignia (Turyen) (1)","(1)","The Blightcaller Uncovered (1)"}},
[6186]={o="Return to Stormwind and inform Highlord Bolvar Fordragon of the fate of Nathanos Marris."},
[6187]={o="Assemble an army and travel to the Eastern Plaguelands. Launch a full assault on Nathanos Blightcaller and any Horde filth that may attempt to protect him. Keep your wits about you, &lt;name&gt;. The Horde will defend the ranger lord with their very lives.",r={"Nathanos Blightcaller (1)"}},
[6261]={o="Bring Osric's Crate to Dungar Longdrink the gryphon master.",s="Osric Strang",e="Dungar Longdrink"},
[6281]={o="Buy a gryphon ride from the gryphon master Thor, then bring Lewis' Note to Osric Strang, in the shop Limited Immunity, in the Old Town of Stormwind.",s="Thor",e="Osric Strang"},
[6282]={o="Maggran Earthbinder in Sun Rock Retreat wants you to slay 7 Bloodfury Harpies, 7 Bloodfury Ambushers, 7 Bloodfury Slayers and 7 Bloodfury Roguefeathers.",r={"Bloodfury Harpy (7)","Bloodfury Ambusher (7)","Bloodfury Slayer (7)","Bloodfury Roguefeather (7)"}},
[6283]={o="Maggran at Sun Rock Retreat wishes you to slay Bloodfury Ripper and bring her remains as proof of your deed.",r={"Bloodfury Ripper's Remains (1)"}},
[6284]={o="Kill Besseleth and bring Besseleth's Fang to Maggran at Sun Rock Retreat.",r={"Besseleth's Fang (1)"}},
[6285]={o="Buy a gryphon ride to Sentinel Hill from the gryphon master Dungar Longdrink, then take Osric's Crate to Lewis at Sentinel Hill.",s="Dungar Longdrink",e="Quartermaster Lewis"},
[6301]={o="Tammra Windfield at Sun Rock Retreat wants you to gather 10 Gaea Seeds.",r={"Gaea Seed (10)"}},
[6321]={o="Bring Podrig's Order to Karos Razok."},
[6322]={o="Bring Gordon's Crate to Michael Garrett."},
[6323]={o="Buy a bat ride to the Undercity from the bat master Karos Razok, then take Podrig's Order to Gordon Wendham in the Undercity."},
[6324]={o="Buy a bat ride to the Sepulcher from the bat master Michael Garrett, then bring Gordon's Crate to Deathguard Podrig in the Sepulcher."},
[6341]={o="Bring Nessa's Collection to Vesprystus.",s="Nessa Shadowsong",e="Vesprystus"},
[6342]={o="Ride a hippogryph to Auberdine from the hippogryph master Vesprystus, then bring Nessa's Collection to Laird.",s="Vesprystus",e="Laird"},
[6343]={o="Bring Laird's Response to Nessa Shadowsong.",s="Laird",e="Nessa Shadowsong"},
[6344]={o="Speak with Nessa Shadowsong.",s="Mydrannul",e="Nessa Shadowsong"},
[6361]={o="Bring the Bundle of Hides to the wind rider master Devrak in the Crossroads."},
[6362]={o="Buy a wind rider to Thunder Bluff from the wind rider master Devrak, then bring the Bundle of Hides to Ahanu in Thunder Bluff."},
[6363]={o="Bring Ahanu's Leather Goods to Tal in Thunder Bluff."},
[6364]={o="Buy a wind rider to the Crossroads from the wind rider master Tal, then bring Ahanu's Leather Goods to Jahan Hawkwing."},
[6365]={o="Bring Zargh's Meats to Devrak in the Crossroads."},
[6381]={o="Plant 10 Gaea Seeds in Gaea Dirt Mounds, and then return the remaining Enchanted Gaea Seeds to Tammra at Sun Rock Retreat.",r={"Gaea seed planted (10)"}},
[6382]={o="Speak with Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale."},
[6383]={o="There are three legendary creatures that make up the Ashenvale Hunt; you may seek them and test yourself against their cunning and might. &nbsp;In the process, you will hopefully learn something about yourself. &nbsp;The creatures are: the bear Ursangous, the nightsaber cat Shadumbra, and the hippogryph Sharptalon. The creatures of the Ashenvale Hunt are powerful, and you may find that you'll need aid in bringing them down. &nbsp;If you should best them, bring me proof of your deed."},
[6384]={o="Buy a wind rider to Orgrimmar from the wind rider master Devrak, then bring Zargh's Meats to Gryshka in Orgrimmar."},
[6385]={o="Bring Gryshka's Letter to Doras in Orgrimmar."},
[6386]={o="Buy a wind rider to the Crossroads from the wind rider master Doras, then bring Gryshka's Letter to Zargh at the Crossroads."},
[6387]={o="Bring Brock's List to Thorgrum Borrelson in Thelsamar.",s="Brock Stoneseeker",e="Thorgrum Borrelson"},
[6388]={o="Bring the Honorary Picks to Gryth Thurden in Ironforge.",s="Golnir Bouldertoe",e="Gryth Thurden"},
[6389]={o="Release the Plagueland Termites in the Northridge Lumber Mill, then return with the Barrel of Plagueland Termites to Nathaniel Dumah at Chillwind Camp in Western Plaguelands."},
[6390]={o="Release the Plagueland Termites in the Northridge Lumber Mill, then return with the Barrel of Plagueland Termites to Mickey Levine at the Bulwark in Tirisfal Glades."},
[6391]={o="Buy a gryphon to Ironforge from the gryphon master Thorgrum Borrelson, then bring Brock's List to Golnir Bouldertoe in Ironforge.",s="Thorgrum Borrelson",e="Golnir Bouldertoe"},
[6392]={o="Buy a gryphon to Thelsamar from the gryphon master Gryth Thurden, then bring the Honorary Picks to Brock Stoneseeker in Thelsamar.",s="Gryth Thurden",e="Brock Stoneseeker"},
[6393]={o="Bring 10 Incendrites to Tsunaman at Sun Rock Retreat.",r={"Incendrites (10)"}},
[6394]={o="Bring Thazz'ril's Pick to Foreman Thazz'ril.",r={"Thazz'ril's Pick (1)"}},
[6395]={o="Bring Samuel Fipps' Remains to Marla's Grave, then return to Novice Elreth.",r={"Samuel's Remains Buried (1)","Samuel's Remains (1)"}},
[6401]={o="Tell Tammra Windfield in Sun Rock Retreat the good news."},
[6402]={o="Travel to Stormwind City and venture to the city gates. Speak with Squire Rowe so that he may let Marshal Windsor know that you have arrived."},
[6403]={o="Follow Reginald Windsor through Stormwind. Protect him from harm!",r={"Reginald's March (1)"}},
[6421]={o="Explore deep into the cave at Boulderslide Ravine and bring back 10 Resonite Crystals for Mor'rogal at Sun Rock Retreat to investigate.",r={"Resonite Crystal (10)","(1)","Investigate Cave in Boulderslide Ravine (1)"}},
[6441]={o="Collect 16 Satyr Horns for Pixel in Splintertree Post.",r={"Satyr Horns (16)"}},
[6442]={o="Bring 20 Wrathtail Heads to Marukai along the Zoram Strand.",r={"Wrathtail Head (20)"}},
[6461]={o="Xen'zilla at Malaka'Jin needs you to kill 10 Deepmoss Creepers and 7 Deepmoss Venomspitters.",r={"Deepmoss Creeper (10)","Deepmoss Venomspitter (7)"}},
[6462]={o="Bring 8 Troll Charms to Mitsuwa at the Zoram'gar Outpost.",r={"Troll Charm (8)"}},
[6481]={o="Open the Resonite cask with the Enchanted Resonite Crystal, and then slay Goggeroc. Return to Mor'rogal with the news and Enchanted Resonite Crystal.",r={"Goggeroc (1)"}},
[6482]={o="Escort Ruul, then speak with Yama Snowhoof in Spintertree Post.",r={"Escort Ruul from the Thistlefurs. (1)"}},
[6501]={o="You must search the world for a being capable of restoring the power to the Fragment of the Dragon's Eye. The only information you possess about such a being is that they exist."},
[6502]={o="You must retrieve the Blood of the Black Dragon Champion from General Drakkisath. Drakkisath can be found in his throne room behind the Halls of Ascension in Blackrock Spire.",r={"Blood of the Black Dragon Champion (1)"}},
[6503]={o="Kill 9 Ashenvale Outrunners, then return to Kuray'bin at Splintertree Outpost.",r={"Ashenvale Outrunner (9)"}},
[6504]={o="Find the 12 missing pages of the Shredder Operating Manual, and put them together to form Chapters 1, 2, and 3. Return the pages to Gurda Ragescar near Splintertree Post.",r={"Shredder Operating Manual - Chapter 1 (1)","Shredder Operating Manual - Chapter 2 (1)","Shredder Operating Manual - Chapter 3 (1)"}},
[6521]={o="Bring Ambassador Malcin's Head to Varimathras in the Undercity.",r={"Ambassador Malcin's Head (1)"}},
[6522]={o="Take the Small Scroll to Varimathras in the Undercity.",r={"Small Scroll (Provided) (1)"},e="Varimathras"},
[6523]={o="Escort Kaya Flathoof to Camp Aparaje, and then return to Makaba Flathoof near the southeastern edge of Stonetalon.",r={"Kaya Escorted to Camp Aparaje (1)"}},
[6541]={o="Report to Kadrak at the watch tower in northern Barrens."},
[6542]={o="Report to Kadrak at the watch tower in northern Barrens."},
[6543]={o="Open the Bundle of Reports. &nbsp;Take the Warsong Reports to the Warsong Scout, Warsong Runner, and Warsong Outrider. Bring back the updates they give you to Kadrak at the northern watch tower in the barrens.",r={"Warsong Scout Update (1)","Warsong Runner Update (1)","Warsong Outrider Update (1)"}},
[6544]={o="Escort Torek on his attack against Silverwing Outpost and Duriel Moonfire, then report to Ertog Ragetusk at Splintertree Post.",r={"Take Silverwing Outpost. (1)"}},
[6545]={o="So you're here with my orders? Always good to see a new recruit with an exuberant nature and a strong will. You'd best learn fast if you expect to keep up here. The threat of the naga grows, &lt;name&gt;. I have observed and have taken up defenses against several attacks on this outpost since I arrived here. But if you'd like to pitch in with that effort, speak with one of the others here at the outpost.",r={"Warsong Report (1)"}},
[6546]={o="Much danger lies along this path, &lt;name&gt;. You'd do best to remember this while traveling in these lands. The threat of the alliance is quite near. We are faced by enemies on all fronts. The satyr are a formidable and prevalent force in eastern Ashenvale. &nbsp;I have also discovered that the naga have taken over a large area of the land of Azshara. It's good to see that we are still bolstering our numbers -- be ready for what lies ahead, &lt;name&gt;.",r={"Warsong Report (1)"}},
[6547]={o="Keep an eye out, &lt;race&gt;. The elves are often hiding in the shadows... We must always be watching. We have worked very hard to claim this land, and the elves are looking for a chance to take it from us. I assume you have my next orders from Kadrak?",r={"Warsong Report (1)"}},
[6548]={o="Kill 8 Grimtotem Ruffians and 6 Grimtotem Mercenaries, and then return to Makaba Flathoof near the southeastern edge of Stonetalon.",r={"Grimtotem Ruffian (8)","Grimtotem Mercenary (6)"}},
[6561]={o="Bring the head of Twilight Lord Kelris to Bashana Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.",r={"Head of Kelris (1)"},s="Argent Guard Thaelrid",e="Bashana Runetotem"},
[6562]={o="Speak to Je'neu Sancrea in Ashenvale.",s="Tsunaman",e="Je'neu Sancrea"},
[6563]={o="Bring 20 Sapphires of Aku'Mai to Je'neu Sancrea in Ashenvale.",r={"Sapphire of Aku'Mai (20)"},s="Je'neu Sancrea",e="Je'neu Sancrea"},
[6564]={o="Bring the Damp Note to Je'neu Sancrea in Ashenvale.",r={"Damp Note (Provided) (1)"},e="Je'neu Sancrea"},
[6565]={o="Kill Lorgus Jett in Blackfathom Deeps and then return to Je'neu Sancrea in Ashenvale.",r={"Lorgus Jett slain (1)"},s="Je'neu Sancrea",e="Je'neu Sancrea"},
[6566]={o="Listen to Thrall.",r={"Thrall's Tale (1)"}},
[6567]={o="Seek out Rexxar. The Warchief has instructed you as to his whereabouts. Search the paths of Desolace, between the Stonetalon Mountains and Feralas."},
[6568]={o="Deliver Rexxar's Testament to Myranda the Hag in the Western Plaguelands."},
[6569]={o="Travel to Blackrock Spire and collect 20 Black Dragonspawn Eyes. Return to Myranda the Hag when the task is complete.",r={"Black Dragonspawn Eye (20)"}},
[6570]={o="Travel to the Wyrmbog in Dustwallow Marsh and seek out Emberstrife's Den. Once inside, wear the Amulet of Draconic Subversion and speak with Emberstrife."},
[6571]={o="Collect the Warsong Supplies: Warsong Saw Blades, Logging Rope, Warsong Oil, and the Warsong Axe Shipment for Locke Okarr in Splintertree Post.",r={"Warsong Saw Blades (1)","Warsong Axe Shipment (1)","Warsong Oil (1)","Logging Rope (1)"}},
[6581]={o="Direct from Ratchet, the Warsong saw blades! Yep, I have them right here. ..But what sort of payment do you have for me? You can't just take them, you know! My time isn't cheap! What I really need is a good gun to carry with me on my travels. A girl's gotta protect herself, you know? There's a gun I really like that I'm sure an engineer would have no problem making. So, if you bring me a deadly blunderbuss, I'll give you the saw blade shipment. Do we have a deal?",r={"Deadly Blunderbuss (1)"}},
[6582]={o="You must find the blue dragonflight drake champion, Scryer, and slay him. Pry his skull from his corpse and return it to Emberstrife. You know that Scryer can be found in Winterspring.",r={"The Skull of Scryer (1)"}},
[6583]={o="Destroy the drake champion of the Green Flight, Somnus. Take his skull and return it to Emberstrife.",r={"The Skull of Somnus (1)"}},
[6584]={o="Guarding the Caverns of Time in the Tanaris Desert is Chronalis, child of Nozdormu. Destroy him and return his skull to Emberstrife.",r={"The Skull of Chronalis (1)"}},
[6585]={o="Travel to Grim Batol and track down Axtroz, drake champion of the Red Flight. Destroy him and take his skull. Return the skull to Emberstrife.",r={"The Skull of Axtroz (1)"}},
[6601]={o="It would appear as if the charade is over. You know that the Amulet of Draconic Subversion that Myranda the Hag created for you will not function inside Blackrock Spire. Perhaps you should find Rexxar and explain your predicament. Show him the Dull Drakefire Amulet. Hopefully he will know what to do next."},
[6602]={o="Travel to Blackrock Spire and slay General Drakkisath. Gather his blood and return it to Rexxar.",r={"Blood of the Black Dragon Champion (1)"}},
[6603]={o="Find Donova Snowden near the hot springs in Winterspring."},
[6604]={o="Speak with Jaron Stoneshaper at Starfall Village."},
[6605]={o="Speak with Winna Hazzard in Felwood."},
[6606]={o="Speak with Witch Doctor Mau'ari in Everlook."},
[6607]={o="Nat Pagle wants you to catch the following fish: Misty Reed Mahi Mahi from the Misty Reed Strand in the Swamp of Sorrows. A Sar'theris Striker from the Sar'theris Strand in Desolace. Feralas Ahi from the Verdantis River of Feralas. Savage Coast Blue Sailfin from the Savage Coast of Stranglethorn Vale. Return to Nat Pagle when you have reeled them all in!",r={"Feralas Ahi (1)","Misty Reed Mahi Mahi (1)","Sar'theris Striker (1)","Savage Coast Blue Sailfin (1)"}},
[6608]={o="You think Lumak is trying to tell you that he can no longer help you improve your fishing skill. You may want to try to find his friend, Nat Pagle, a human fishing off one of the islands south of Theramore (at least that's what you think Lumak said)."},
[6609]={o="Travel to Kalimdor, to the coastal city of Theramore. From there you must search for an island, south of the main town. Nat Pagle awaits your arrival!"},
[6610]={o="Dirge Quikcleave wants you to get the following items: 12 Giant Eggs. You will find those on the Rocs wandering Tanaris or any other species of large bird. 10 pieces of Zesty Clam Meat. You can find those in clams, naturally! 20 pieces of Alterac Swiss. Get thee to a cheesery! Gather all of the items and return to Dirge.",r={"Giant Egg (12)","Zesty Clam Meat (10)","Alterac Swiss (20)"}},
[6611]={o="Travel to Gadgetzan in the Tanaris desert and speak with Dirge Quikcleave about advancing your cooking career."},
[6612]={o="Travel to Gadgetzan in the Tanaris desert and speak with Dirge Quikcleave about advancing your cooking career."},
[6621]={o="Place Karang's Banner on the Foulweald Totem Mound. &nbsp;Do not let the furbolgs destroy the banner. &nbsp;Defeat Chief Murgut and bring Murgut's Totem to Karang Amakkar at Zoram'gar.",r={"Murgut's Totem (1)"}},
[6622]={o="Save patients by using Triage Bandages to tend to their wounds. You must save 15 patients before 6 of them die from their injuries. Remember the order of triage! Critically Injured Soldiers die the fastest followed by Badly Injured Soldiers. Injured Soldiers take the longest to die and should be saved AFTER your Critically Injured and Badly Injured Soldiers have been triaged.",r={"15 Patients Saved! (1)"}},
[6623]={o="Travel to Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands and speak with Doctor Gregory Victor about joining the ranks of Horde Trauma."},
[6624]={o="Save patients by using Triage Bandages to tend to their wounds. You must save 15 patients before 6 of them die from their injuries. Remember the order of triage! Critically Injured Soldiers die the fastest followed by Badly Injured Soldiers. Injured Soldiers take the longest to die and should be saved AFTER your Critically Injured and Badly Injured Soldiers have been triaged.",r={"15 Patients Saved! (1)"}},
[6625]={o="Travel to Theramore in the Dustwallow Marsh and speak with Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen about joining the ranks of Alliance Trauma."},
[6626]={o="Kill 8 Razorfen Battleguard, 8 Razorfen Thornweavers, and 8 Death's Head Cultists and return to Myriam Moonsinger near the entrance to Razorfen Downs.",r={"Razorfen Battleguard (8)","Razorfen Thornweaver (8)","Death's Head Cultist (8)"}},
[6627]={o="Answer Braug Dimspirit's question successfully and then speak to him again. He will remain in Stonetalon Mountains when you are ready.",r={"Answer Braug Dimspirit's question correctly (1)"}},
[6628]={o="Answer Parqual Fintallas' question successfully and then speak to him again. He will remain in the Undercity until you are ready.",r={"Answer Parqual Fintallas' question correctly (1)"}},
[6629]={o="Kill Grundig Darkcloud and 6 Grimtotem Brutes, and return to Makaba Flathoof near the southeastern edge of Stonetalon.",r={"Grundig Darkcloud (1)","Grimtotem Brute (6)"}},
[6641]={o="Keep Muglash safe as he travels to the brazier. Help him by putting the brazier out, then protect him as you fight against the Naga. If you are successful, return to the Zoram'gar Outpost and inform the Warsong Runner of the death of Vorsha the Lasher.",r={"Defeat Vorsha the Lasher (1)"}},
[6642]={o="Dark Iron, while plentiful in the Depths, is still a valued commodity amongst the Brotherhood. The sacred arms and armaments of Ragnaros favor Dark Iron. For every 10 pieces of Dark Iron Ore you offer, favor amongst the Brotherhood you will gain.",r={"Dark Iron Ore (10)"}},
[6643]={o="Woe unto those that tempt fate inside the Molten Core. Death comes swiftly - the punishment dealt without mercy. Many of the Brotherhood have been lost in their search for Fiery Cores. Offer 1 Fiery Core and you shall be granted favor amongst the Brotherhood.",r={"Fiery Core (1)"}},
[6644]={o="The Thorium Brotherhood sympathizes with your plight, &lt;race&gt;. This is why Lokthos has been empowered to bargain. Offer 1 Lava Core and you shall be granted favor amongst the Brotherhood.",r={"Lava Core (1)"}},
[6645]={o="Many of the sacred recipes require the skin from Ragnaros' chosen pets. Offer 2 Core Leather, skinned from the smoldering corpses of the Core Hounds of the Molten Core and you shall be granted favor amongst the Brotherhood.",r={"Core Leather (2)"}},
[6646]={o="The tears of the Fire Lord are a rare find indeed. Offer 1 Blood of the Mountain and you shall be granted favor amongst the Brotherhood.",r={"Blood of the Mountain (1)"}},
[6661]={o="Capture 5 Deeprun Rats by using the Rat Catcher's Flute. Lead the rats back to Monty. Don't forget to turn in the flute when you're finished.",r={"Rats captured (5)"}},
[6662]={o="Take the Carton of Mystery Meat to Nipsy at the Stormwind Deeprun Tram Depot."},
[6681]={o="Take the Seal of Ravenholdt to Fahrad at Ravenholdt Manor, hidden away in the hills of Hillsbrad. Your cunning will be tested along the way. Be prepared.",r={"Rite of Cunning (1)"},e="Fahrad"},
[6701]={o="We have been entrenched in a battle with the Syndicate for years. What they lack in skill they make up for in numbers. It's impossible to kill them off fast enough to have any noticeable impact on their population! We've found that the best way to deal with their size is to pilfer their emblems. Once an emblem is stolen the shamed member is 'dealt' with internally. Pick their pockets clean and turn the emblems in to me or one of the other guards. Start at Durnholde, south of here.",r={"Syndicate Emblem (1)"}},
[6721]={o="Speak with Dazalar in Dolanaar.",s="Olmin Burningbeard",e="Dazalar"},
[6722]={o="Speak with Dazalar in Dolanaar.",s="Grif Wildheart",e="Dazalar"},
[6761]={o="Speak with Mathrengyl Bearwalker at the Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus."},
[6762]={o="Speak with Rabine Saturna in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade. &nbsp;Moonglade lies between Felwood and Winterspring, accessible through a path out of Timbermaw Hold."},
[6804]={o="Use the Aspect of Neptulon on poisoned elementals of Eastern Plaguelands. &nbsp;Bring 12 Discordant Bracers and the Aspect of Neptulon to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.",r={"Discordant Bracers (12)"}},
[6805]={o="Kill 15 Dust Stormers and 15 Desert Rumbers and then return to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.",r={"Dust Stormer (15)","Desert Rumbler (15)"}},
[6821]={o="Bring the Eye of the Emberseer to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.",r={"Eye of the Emberseer (1)"}},
[6822]={o="Kill 1 Fire Lord, 1 Molten Giant, 1 Ancient Core Hound and 1 Lava Surger, then return to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.",r={"Molten Giant (1)","Firelord (1)","Ancient Core Hound (1)","Lava Surger (1)"}},
[6823]={o="Earn an Honored faction with the Hydraxian Waterlords, then talk to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.",r={"Hydraxian Waterlords: (1)"}},
[6824]={o="Bring the Hands of Lucifron, Sulfuron, Gehennas and Shazzrah to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.",r={"Hand of Shazzrah (1)","Hand of Lucifron (1)","Hand of Gehennas (1)","Hand of Sulfuron (1)"}},
[6844]={o="Take the Encrusted Silithid Object to Umber - the Cenarion Circle's archivist - in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade."},
[6845]={o="Speak with Rabine Saturna in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade."},
[6921]={o="Bring the Fathom Core to Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost, Ashenvale.",r={"Fathom Core (1)"},s="Je'neu Sancrea",e="Je'neu Sancrea"},
[6922]={o="Bring the Strange Water Globe to Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost, Ashenvale.",r={"Strange Water Globe (Provided) (1)"},e="Je'neu Sancrea"},
[6981]={o="Travel to Ratchet to find someone that can tell you more about the glowing shard.Then, deliver the shard as you are directed.",r={"Glowing Shard (Provided) (1)","Speak with someone in Ratchet about the Glowing Shard (1)"},e="Falla Sagewind"},
[7003]={o="Use Zorbin's Ultra-Shrinker to zap any kind of giant found in Feralas into a more manageable form. &nbsp;Bring 15 Miniaturization Residues found on the zapped versions of these giants to Zorbin Fandazzle at the docks of the Forgotten Coast, Feralas.",r={"Miniaturization Residue (15)"}},
[7028]={o="Collect 25 Theradric Crystal Carvings for Willow in Desolace.",r={"Theradric Crystal Carving (25)"}},
[7029]={o="Fill the Coated Cerulean Vial at the orange crystal pool in Maraudon. Use the Filled Cerulean Vial on the Vylestem Vines to force the corrupted Noxxious Scion to emerge. Heal 8 plants by killing these Noxxious Scion, then return to Vark Battlescar in Shadowprey Village.",r={"Vylestem Vines healed (8)","Filled Cerulean Vial (1)"}},
[7041]={o="Fill the Coated Cerulean Vial at the orange crystal pool in Maraudon. Use the Filled Cerulean Vial on the Vylestem Vines to force the corrupted Noxxious Scion to emerge. Heal 8 plants by killing these Noxxious Scion, then return to Talendria in Nijel's Point.",r={"Vylestem Vines healed (8)","Filled Cerulean Vial (1)"}},
[7044]={o="Recover the two parts of the Scepter of Celebras: the Celebrian Rod and the Celebrian Diamond. Find a way to speak with Celebras.",r={"Celebrian Diamond (1)","Celebrian Rod (1)"}},
[7046]={o="Assist Celebras the Redeemed while he creates the Scepter of Celebras. Speak with him when the ritual is complete.",r={"Create the Scepter of Celebras (1)"}},
[7064]={o="Slay Princess Theradras and return to Selendra near Shadowprey Village in Desolace.",r={"Princess Theradras (1)"}},
[7065]={o="Slay Princess Theradras and return to Keeper Marandis at Nijel's Point in Desolace.",r={"Princess Theradras (1)"}},
[7066]={o="Seek out Remulos in Moonglade and give him the Seed of Life."},
[7067]={o="Read the Pariah's Instructions. Afterwards, obtain the Amulet of Union from Maraudon and return it to the Centaur Pariah in southern Desolace.",r={"Amulet of Union (1)","Amulet of Spirits (1)"}},
[7068]={o="Collect 10 Shadowshard Fragments from Maraudon and return them to Uthel'nay in Orgrimmar.",r={"Shadowshard Fragment (10)"}},
[7070]={o="Collect 10 Shadowshard Fragments from Maraudon and return them to Archmage Tervosh in Theramore on the coast of Dustwallow Marsh.",r={"Shadowshard Fragment (10)"}},
[7201]={o="Travel to Blackrock Depths and recover 10 Essence of the Elements. Your first inclination is to search the golems and golem makers. You remember Vivian Lagrave also muttering something about elementals.",r={"Essence of the Elements (10)"}},
[7321]={o="Bring 10 pieces of Turtle Meat and some Soothing Spices to Christoph Jeffcoat in Tarren Mill.",r={"Turtle Meat (10)","Soothing Spices (1)"}},
[7341]={o="Greetings, &lt;race&gt;. I am Kolark, Bounty &lt;class&gt; from Thunderbluff. Much of the world I have traveled and much I have seen. My journeys across the South Seas led to the discovery of these wonderous thorium headed arrows. Alas, I have an endless supply of the arrows but have exhausted my supply of shells. Bah, no self respecting Tauren would ever be caught dead using a flimsy bow. The arrows are useless! I will offer a trade: An even exchange of thorium shells for my thorium headed arrows. Deal?",r={"Thorium Shells (200)"}},
[7342]={o="Can you believe this rubbish?! The last shipment of ammunition from Kharanos was botched! All we have for ammo now are these flimsy, good for nothing arrows! What in the world am I going to do with 500,000 thorium headed arrows? I'll tell you what, kid. If you can bring me thorium shells, I'll trade you thorium headed arrows - straight up! Deal?",r={"Thorium Shells (200)"}},
[7383]={o="Fill the Amethyst Phial and bring it back to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.",r={"Filled Amethyst Phial (1)"},s="Corithras Moonrage",e="Corithras Moonrage"},
[7429]={o="It's called the Gordok Shackle Key - well, that's what these \"tons o' fun\" keep calling it. &nbsp;I think any of the ogres might have it, but I'm not sure if any specific ones do. &nbsp;Maybe the guards have a better chance of having one... What am I talking about - you have it already, don't you?! &nbsp;Is that it there??!",r={"Gordok Shackle Key (1)"}},
[7441]={o="Travel to Dire Maul and locate the Imp, Pusillin. Convince Pusillin to give you Azj'Tordin's Book of Incantations through any means necessary. Return to Azj'Tordin at the Lariss Pavilion in Feralas should you recover the Book of Incantations.",r={"Book of Incantations (1)"}},
[7461]={o="You must destroy the guardians surrounding the 5 Pylons that power the Prison of Immol'thar. Once the Pylons have powered down, the force field surrounding Immol'thar will have dissipated. Enter the Prison of Immol'thar and eradicate the foul demon that stands at its heart. Finally, confront Prince Tortheldrin in Athenaeum. Return to the Shen'dralar Ancient in the courtyard should you complete this quest.",r={"Immol'thar (1)","Prince Tortheldrin (1)"}},
[7462]={o="Return to the Athenaeum and find the Treasure of the Shen'dralar. Claim your reward!"},
[7463]={o="Travel to the Warpwood Quarter of Dire Maul and slay the water elemental, Hydrospawn. Return to Lorekeeper Lydros in the Athenaeum with the Hydrospawn Essence.",r={"Hydrospawn Essence (1)"}},
[7481]={o="Search Dire Maul for Kariel Winthalus. Report back to Sage Korolusk at Camp Mojache with whatever information that you may find.",r={"Master Kariel Winthalus Found (1)"}},
[7482]={o="Search Dire Maul for Kariel Winthalus. Report back to Scholar Runethorn at Feathermoon with whatever information that you may find.",r={"Master Kariel Winthalus Found (1)"}},
[7483]={o="Bring a Libram of Rapidity, 1 Pristine Black Diamond, 2 Large Brilliant Shards, and 2 Blood of Heroes to Lorekeeper Lydros in Dire Maul to receive an Arcanum of Rapidity.",r={"Libram of Rapidity (1)","Pristine Black Diamond (1)","Large Brilliant Shard (2)","Blood of Heroes (2)"}},
[7484]={o="Bring a Libram of Focus, 1 Pristine Black Diamond, 4 Large Brilliant Shards, and 2 Skin of Shadow to Lorekeeper Lydros in Dire Maul to receive an Arcanum of Focus.",r={"Libram of Focus (1)","Pristine Black Diamond (1)","Large Brilliant Shard (4)","Skin of Shadow (2)"}},
[7485]={o="Bring a Libram of Protection, 1 Pristine Black Diamond, 2 Large Brilliant Shards, and 1 Frayed Abomination Stitching to Lorekeeper Lydros in Dire Maul to receive an Arcanum of Protection.",r={"Libram of Protection (1)","Pristine Black Diamond (1)","Large Brilliant Shard (2)","Frayed Abomination Stitching (1)"}},
[7486]={o="Claim your reward from Hydraxis' Coffer."},
[7487]={o="Venture to the Molten Core entry portal in Blackrock Depths and recover a Core Fragment. Return to Lothos Riftwaker in Blackrock Mountain when you have recovered the Core Fragment.",r={"Core Fragment (1)"}},
[7488]={o="Bring Lethtendris' Web to Latronicus Moonspear at the Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas.",r={"Lethtendris's Web (1)"}},
[7489]={o="Bring Lethtendris's Web to Talo Thornhoof at Camp Mojache in Feralas.",r={"Lethtendris's Web (1)"}},
[7490]={o="Take the Head of Onyxia to Thrall in Orgrimmar."},
[7491]={o="Seek out Overlord Runthak in the Valley of Strength."},
[7492]={o="Speak with Talo Thornhoof at Camp Mojache in Feralas."},
[7493]={o="A dragon slayer and a seasoned leatherworker? You do not cease to astonish, hero. I am humbled. Please accept what I am about to teach you. This knowledge will prove to be invaluable if you are to destroy what remains of the Black Dragonflight. Create the cloak from the scales of the brood mother. It will protect you and your allies against the incendiary breath of the Lord of Blackrock... Nefarian."},
[7494]={o="Speak with Latronicus Moonspear at the Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas."},
[7495]={o="Take the Head of Onyxia to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind."},
[7496]={o="Seek out Major Mattingly in the Valley of Heroes."},
[7497]={o="A dragon slayer and a seasoned leatherworker? You do not cease to astonish, hero. I am humbled. Please accept what I am about to teach you. This knowledge will prove to be invaluable if you are to destroy what remains of the Black Dragonflight. Create the cloak from the scales of the brood mother. It will protect you and your allies against the incendiary breath of the Lord of Blackrock... Nefarian."},
[7498]={o="Return the book to its rightful owners."},
[7499]={o="Return the book to its rightful owners."},
[7500]={o="Return the book to its rightful owners."},
[7501]={o="Return the book to its rightful owners."},
[7502]={o="Return the book to its rightful owners."},
[7503]={o="Return the book to its rightful owners."},
[7504]={o="Return the book to its rightful owners."},
[7505]={o="Return the book to its rightful owners."},
[7506]={o="Return the book to its rightful owners."},
[7507]={o="Return Foror's Compendium of Dragon Slaying to the Athenaeum."},
[7508]={o="Give the Dull and Flat Elven Blade to Lorekeeper Lydros."},
[7509]={o="You must get Onyxia to breathe fire on the Unfired Ancient Blade. Once this is done, pick up the now Heated Ancient Blade. Be warned, a Heated Ancient Blade will not remain heated forever - time is of the essence. The last step before returning to me is to slay the beast and drive the Heated Ancient Blade into her corpse. Do this and Quel'Serrar will be yours.",r={"Treated Ancient Blade (1)","Heated Ancient Blade (1)"}},
[7541]={o="It will take time for our scholars to study the pendant you brought us. &nbsp;But for your service to the Horde I would like to offer you a small token. Thank you, &lt;name&gt;. &nbsp;Your acts bring honor to you, and to us."},
[7562]={o="Speak with Mor'zul Bloodbringer in the Burning Steppes."},
[7563]={o="Bring 30 bottles of Raging Beast's Blood to Mor'zul Bloodbringer in the Burning Steppes.",r={"Raging Beast's Blood (30)"}},
[7564]={o="Bring the Case of Blood to Gorzeeki Wildeyes in the Burning Steppes."},
[7581]={o="Travel to Dire Maul in Feralas and recover 15 Satyr Blood from the Wildspawn Satyr that inhabit the Warpwood Quarter. Return to Daio in the Tainted Scar when this is done.",r={"Satyr Blood (15)"}},
[7582]={o="Travel to Darkwhisper Gorge in Winterspring and recover 5 Tears of the Hederine from the Hederine demons that occupy the gorge. Return to Daio in the Tainted Scar when you have completed this task.",r={"Tears of the Hederine (5)"}},
[7583]={o="Venture forth into the Tainted Scar and locate a Doomguard Commander. Use the Glowing Crystal Prison on the Doomguard Commander. Be prepared for a ferocious onslaught of attacks, as the demon attempts to escape capture. Should you succeed, return the Imprisoned Doomguard to Daio in the Tainted Scar.",r={"Imprisoned Doomguard (1)"}},
[7601]={o="Speak with Impsy in Felwood."},
[7602]={o="Impsy in Felwood has asked that you bring him three Flawless Fel Essences originating from three distinct locations. The Legashi Satyrs of Azshara hold the Flawless Fel Essence of their region. The Jaedenar Legionnaires of Jaedenar hold the Flawless Fel Essence of their region. The Felguard Sentries of the Blasted Lands hold the Flawless Fel Essence of their region. Recover the Flawless Fel Essences and return &nbsp;to Impsy in Felwood.",r={"Flawless Fel Essence (Azshara) (1)","Flawless Fel Essence (Jaedenar) (1)","Flawless Fel Essence (Dark Portal) (1)"}},
[7603]={o="Search Shatter Scar Vale in Felwood for the remains of Kroshius. When you locate the remains, use the Fel Fire near them and await Kroshius' return. When the infernal has awoken, slay him and take from his corpse Kroshius' Infernal Core. Return Kroshius' Infernal Core to Niby the Almighty in Felwood.",r={"Kroshius' Infernal Core (1)"}},
[7604]={o="Turn the Thorium Brotherhood Contract in to Lokhtos Darkbargainer if you would like to receive the plans for Sulfuron.",r={"Sulfuron Ingot (1)"}},
[7621]={o="&lt;class&gt;, you are about to undergo a rigorous series of events which shall test all of your abilities. I suggest that you listen to the story that I have to tell. Be warned, you must complete this task alone. It is recommended that your allies remain at a distance. Interference by outside agents will result in a most severe punishment. Destiny has led you and you alone here. Battle with honor. Harness the Light."},
[7622]={o="Save 50 Peasants before 15 are slain. Speak with Eris Havenfire should you accomplish this task. You may view the Death Post to view how many Peasants have been slain.",r={"The Balance of Light and Shadow (1)"}},
[7623]={o="Purchase Shadowy Potions from Gorzeeki in the Burning Steppes. Use the potions to travel through Jaedenar, and speak with Lord Banehollow."},
[7624]={o="Confront Ulathek, then bring The Traitor's Heart to Lord Banehollow in Jaedenar.",r={"The Traitor's Heart (1)"}},
[7625]={o="Purchase Xorothian Stardust from Ur'dan. &nbsp;Bring it to Gorzeeki Wildeyes in the Burning Steppes.",r={"Xorothian Stardust (1)"}},
[7626]={o="Bring 10 Elixirs of Shadow Power to Gorzeeki Wildeyes in the Burning Steppes.",r={"Elixir of Shadow Power (10)"}},
[7627]={o="Bring 6 Large Brilliant Shards and 25 Dark Iron Ore to Gorzeeki in the Burning Steppes.",r={"Large Brilliant Shard (6)","Dark Iron Ore (25)"}},
[7628]={o="Bring 35 Black Dragonscales to Gorzeeki Wildeyes in the Burning Steppes.",r={"Black Dragonscale (35)"}},
[7629]={o="Bring the Imp in a Jar to the alchemy lab in the Scholomance. &nbsp;After the parchment is created, return the jar to Gorzeeki Wildeyes.",r={"Parchment Created (1)"}},
[7630]={o="Bring 3 Arcanite Bars to Gorzeeki in the Burning Steppes.",r={"Arcanite Bar (3)"}},
[7631]={o="Read Mor'zul's Instructions. &nbsp;Summon a Xorothian Dreadsteed, defeat it, then bind its spirit to you."},
[7632]={o="Find the owner of the Ancient Petrified Leaf. Good luck, &lt;name&gt;; It's a big world."},
[7633]={o="Your diligence and integrity has been noted, &lt;class&gt;. We are Ancients: Protectors of this once great forest. Our physical forms were destroyed 10,000 years ago when Archimonde and the Burning Legion marched upon Hyjal. Our spirits, however, remain intact. There are tasks that we can offer. Tasks that if completed will open up the secrets of the Ancients to you. Know this, should you complete these tasks, merely return to this rock and we shall answer the calling."},
[7634]={o="Hastat the Ancient has asked that you bring him a Mature Blue Dragon Sinew. Should you find this sinew, return it to Hastat in Felwood.",r={"Mature Blue Dragon Sinew (1)"}},
[7635]={o="Stoma the Ancient has asked that you bring him a Mature Black Dragon Sinew. Should you find this sinew, return it to Stoma in Felwood.",r={"Mature Black Dragon Sinew (1)"}},
[7636]={o="You must find and destroy these four demonic corrupters: Simone the Seductress. Klinfran the Crazed. Solenor the Slayer. Artorius the Doombringer. Destroy these creatures and return to Vartrus the Ancient in Felwood with their heads. Refer to the Petrified Bark in your inventory for clues as to their whereabouts. You MUST complete this task by yourself.",r={"Simone's Head (1)","Klinfran's Head (1)","Solenor's Head (1)","Artorius's Head (1)"}},
[7637]={o="Travel to Ironforge and get High Priest Rohan's Exorcism Censer. &nbsp;You will need to make a donation of 150 gold in order to secure it.",r={"Money: 150 &nbsp; (1)"}},
[7638]={o="Speak with Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in Stormwind's Cathedral District."},
[7639]={o="Return the Exorcism Censer to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in the Cathedral District of Stormwind."},
[7640]={o="Use the Exorcism Censer to drive out the spirits that torment Terrordale. &nbsp;When you have slain 25 Terrordale Spirits, return to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in the Cathedral District of Stormwind.",r={"Terrordale Spirit (25)"}},
[7641]={o="Speak with Grimand Elmore in Stormwind's Dwarven District."},
[7642]={o="Bring 40 Runecloth, 6 Arcanite Bars, 10 Arthas' Tears, 5 Stratholme Holy Water vials, and 150 gold to Grimand Elmore in the Dwarven District of Stormwind.",r={"Stratholme Holy Water (5)","Arthas' Tears (10)","Runecloth (40)","Arcanite Bar (6)","Money: 150 &nbsp; (1)"}},
[7643]={o="Acquire special horse feed used for feeding a spirit horse. &nbsp;Merideth Carlson in Southshore apparently is the source for such food. Travel to the Dire Maul dungeon in Feralas and slay Tendris Warpwood. &nbsp;Doing so will free the Ancient Equine Spirit. &nbsp;Feed it the special horse feed, thereby soothing the spirit. &nbsp;Finally, give it the Arcanite Barding so it may bless it.",r={"Manna-Enriched Horse Feed (1)"}},
[7644]={o="Return with the Blessed Arcanite Barding to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in the Cathedral District of Stormwind."},
[7645]={o="Retrieve 20 Enriched Manna Biscuits - the key ingredient in making Manna-Enriched Horse Feed - for Merideth Carlson at Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills. &nbsp;The Argent Dawn is known as the sole purveyor of the biscuits. You also need to give her 50 gold to soothe her ruffled sensibilities.",r={"Enriched Manna Biscuit (20)","Money: 50 &nbsp; (1)"}},
[7646]={o="Bring an Azerothian Diamond and a Pristine Black Diamond to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in the Cathedral District of Stormwind.",r={"Azerothian Diamond (1)","Pristine Black Diamond (1)"}},
[7647]={o="Use the Divination Scryer in the heart of the Great Ossuary's basement in the Scholomance. &nbsp;Doing so will bring forth the spirits you must judge. &nbsp;Defeating these spirits will summon forth Death Knight Darkreaver. &nbsp;Defeat him and reclaim the lost soul of the fallen charger. Give the Charger's Redeemed Soul and the Blessed Enchanted Barding to Darkreaver's Fallen Charger.",r={"Charger's Redeemed Soul (1)","Blessed Arcanite Barding (1)","Charger's Lost Soul (1)","Divination Scryer (1)"}},
[7648]={o="Take the Arcanite Barding to Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in Stormwind's Cathedral District for his inspection."},
[7649]={o="Return the book to its rightful owners."},
[7650]={o="Return the book to its rightful owners."},
[7651]={o="Return the book to its rightful owners."},
[7652]={o="Aright, mister, I got a hot deal for ya. I'm lookin' to offload some of these here Imperial plate armor recipes and need someone willing to take on the burden. All I want in exchange is some thorium bars. Sound good?"},
[7653]={o="For the belt plans, I'll be needin' 20 thorium bars.",r={"Thorium Bar (20)"}},
[7654]={o="For the boot plans, I'll be needin' 40 thorium bars. Yep, 40. Are you gonna cry? Would you like a hanky? &lt;Derotain laughs.&gt;",r={"Thorium Bar (40)"}},
[7655]={o="For the bracer plans, I'll be needin' 20 thorium bars. Are you alright, sonny? Yer getting' all red.",r={"Thorium Bar (20)"}},
[7656]={o="For the chest piece plans, I'll be needin' 60 thorium bars. Oh boy, there you go again. Are you gonna be runnin' to yer blue Gods, askin' why they have forsaken you?!? Toughen up, Nancy! Nobody ever said life's fair.",r={"Thorium Bar (60)"}},
[7657]={o="Just hand over 50 thorium bars and the helm plans are yers.",r={"Thorium Bar (50)"}},
[7658]={o="Just hand over 60 thorium bars and the leg plans are yers. I know, I'm driving you into bankruptcy! I've heard it all before so you can save your sob story, weakling.",r={"Thorium Bar (60)"}},
[7659]={o="For the shoulder plans, I'll be needin' 20 thorium bars.",r={"Thorium Bar (20)"}},
[7660]={r={"Horn of the Arctic Wolf (1)"}},
[7661]={r={"Horn of the Red Wolf (1)"}},
[7662]={r={"Teal Kodo (1)"}},
[7663]={r={"Green Kodo (1)"}},
[7664]={r={"Whistle of the Ivory Raptor (1)"}},
[7665]={r={"Whistle of the Mottled Red Raptor (1)"}},
[7666]={o="Are you headed back into the Scholomance, &lt;name&gt;? &nbsp;You've already paid such a great price for the use of the Divination Scryer - perhaps you'd like to take another one with you. &nbsp;With it, you'd be able to face the perils of the Great Ossuary once more. By all means, have it. &nbsp;You've certainly earned it."},
[7667]={o="If you are interested in helping Sagorne Crestrider in Orgrimmar's Valley of Wisdom, bring him an Azerothian Diamond and a Pristine Black Diamond.",r={"Azerothian Diamond (1)","Pristine Black Diamond (1)"}},
[7668]={o="Use the Divination Scryer in the heart of the Great Ossuary's basement in the Scholomance. &nbsp;Doing so will bring forth spirits you must fight. &nbsp;Defeating these spirits will summon forth Death Knight Darkreaver; defeat him. Bring Darkreaver's Head to Sagorne Creststrider in the Valley of Wisdom, Orgrimmar.",r={"Darkreaver's Head (1)"}},
[7669]={o="Are you headed back into the Scholomance, &lt;name&gt;? &nbsp;You've already paid such a great price for the use of the Divination Scryer - perhaps you'd like to take another one with you. &nbsp;With it, you'd be able to face the perils of the Great Ossuary once more. By all means, have it. &nbsp;You've certainly earned it."},
[7670]={o="Speak with Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in Stormwind's Cathedral District."},
[7671]={r={"Reins of the Frostsaber (1)"}},
[7672]={r={"Reins of the Nightsaber (1)"}},
[7673]={r={"Frost Ram (1)"}},
[7674]={r={"Black Ram (1)"}},
[7675]={r={"Icy Blue Mechanostrider Mod A (1)"}},
[7676]={r={"White Mechanostrider Mod A (1)"}},
[7677]={r={"White Stallion Bridle (1)"}},
[7678]={r={"Palomino Bridle (1)"}},
[7681]={o="Feed your pet, then talk to your questgiver."},
[7682]={o="Feed your pet, then talk to your questgiver."},
[7701]={o="Deep within the Slag Pit of the Cauldron, in the Searing Gorge, you will find the traitorous Dark Iron dwarf named Overseer Maltorius. Slay Overseer Maltorius and take his head. Return the head to Lookout Captain Lolo Longstriker in the Searing Gorge for your reward.",r={"Head of Overseer Maltorius (1)"}},
[7703]={o="Find the Gauntlet of Gordok Might and return it to Captain Kromcrush in Dire Maul. According to Kromcrush, the \"old timey story\" says that Tortheldrin - a \"creepy\" elf who called himself a prince - stole it from one of the Gordok kings.",r={"Gauntlet of Gordok Might (1)"}},
[7704]={o="Take Chambermaid Pillaclencher's Pillow to Evonice Sootsmoker in the Searing Gorge."},
[7721]={o="Collect 10 Water Elemental Cores from the Sea Elementals and Sea Sprays along the Forgotten Coast of Feralas, and bring them back to Zorbin Fandazzle who is near the dock there.",r={"Water Elemental Core (10)"}},
[7722]={o="Somewhere in the Slag Pit of the Cauldron you will find the Secret Plans: Fiery Flux that Overseer Maltorius stole. Find those plans and return them to Master Smith Burninate in the Searing Gorge.",r={"Secret Plans: Fiery Flux (1)"}},
[7723]={o="Hansel Heavyhands wants you to kill 20 Heavy War Golems. The Heavy War Golems wander the areas surrounding the Cauldron in the Searing Gorge. When you've killed enough, return to Hansel in Searing Gorge.",r={"Heavy War Golem (20)"}},
[7724]={o="Hansel Heavyhands wants you to kill 20 Greater Lava Spiders in the Searing Gorge. You can find Greater Lava Spiders in the plateaus and lava pools of the Searing Gorge. Return to Hansel Heavyhands in the Searing Gorge when you have killed enough Greater Lava Spiders.",r={"Searing Lava Spider (20)"}},
[7725]={o="Use Zorbin's Ultra-Shrinker to zap any kind of giant found in Feralas into a more manageable form. &nbsp;Bring 10 Miniaturization Residues found on the zapped versions of these giants to Zorbin Fandazzle at the docks of the Forgotten Coast, Feralas.",r={"Miniaturization Residue (10)"}},
[7726]={o="Collect 6 Water Elemental Cores from the Sea Elementals and Sea Sprays along the Forgotten Coast of Feralas, and bring them back to Zorbin Fandazzle who is near the dock there.",r={"Water Elemental Core (6)"}},
[7727]={o="Hansel Heavyhands wants you to kill 20 Incendosaurs. You will find Incendosaurs occupying the lava pools inside the Slag Pit. The Slag Pit can be found in the Cauldron of the Searing Gorge. Return to Hansel Heavyhands in the Searing Gorge when you have killed enough Incendosaurs.",r={"Incendosaur (20)"}},
[7728]={o="Find and return the Smithing Tuyere and Lookout's Spyglass to Taskmaster Scrange in the Searing Gorge. The only information you have about these items is the following: They were definitely stolen by Dark Iron dwarves. The Smithing Tuyere is a blacksmithing tool used by blacksmiths and the Lookout's Spyglass is an invaluable monitoring tool to lookouts.",r={"Smithing Tuyere (1)","Lookout's Spyglass (1)"}},
[7729]={o="Slay 15 Dark Iron Taskmasters and 15 Dark Iron Slavers. Return to Taskmaster Scrange in the Searing Gorge once you have accomplished this task.",r={"Dark Iron Taskmaster (15)","Dark Iron Slaver (15)"}},
[7730]={o="Bring 20 Zukk'ash Carapaces to Hadoken Swiftstrider at Camp Mojache, Feralas.",r={"Zukk'ash Carapace (20)"}},
[7731]={o="Defeat Stinglasher in the Writhing Deep, bringing its glands back to Hadoken Swiftstrider at Camp Mojache, Feralas.",r={"Stinglasher's Glands (1)"}},
[7732]={o="Deliver the Camp Mojache Zukk'ash Report to Zilzibin Drumlore. &nbsp;He resides in the Drag of Orgrimmar."},
[7733]={o="Bring 10 Rage Scar Yeti Hides to Pratt McGrubben at Feathermoon Stronghold, Feralas.",r={"Rage Scar Yeti Hide (10)"}},
[7734]={o="Bring 10 Rage Scar Yeti Hides to Jangdor Swiftstrider at Camp Mojache, Feralas.",r={"Rage Scar Yeti Hide (10)"}},
[7735]={o="Bring the Pristine Yeti Hide to Pratt McGrubben at the Feathermoon Stronghold, Feralas."},
[7736]={o="Let's not waste more of my precious time with jibber jabber, &lt;race&gt;. It's time to focus on replenishing our dwindling fiery flux supply. What I'm gonna need from you is the following: *Incendosaur scales. *Kingsblood. *Coal. I'll take all that you can offer! And you'll do it fast if you wanna get in good with the Brotherhood.",r={"Incendosaur Scale (2)","Kingsblood (4)","Coal (1)"}},
[7737]={o="You've worked your way up through the Brotherhood's corporate hierarchy, &lt;race&gt;. We have begun to look favorably upon you. Quite an accomplishment! If you're interested in more work and earning more respect amongst us, listen up. We can refine the fiery flux by adding a simple Dark Iron residue to the mix. The Dark Iron residue can be found in Blackrock Depths. Bring me all the Dark Iron residue you find!",r={"Dark Iron Residue (4)"}},
[7738]={o="Bring the Perfect Yeti Hide to Jangdor Swiftstrider at Camp Mojache, Feralas."},
[7761]={o="That is one stupid orc. It would appear as if you need to find this brand and gain the Mark of Drakkisath in order to access the Orb of Command. The letter indicates that General Drakkisath guards the brand. Perhaps you should investigate."},
[7781]={o="Return the Head of Nefarian to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind."},
[7782]={o="Venture to the Valley of Heroes in Stormwind City and speak with Field Marshal Afrasiabi."},
[7783]={o="Return the Head of Nefarian to Thrall in Orgrimmar."},
[7784]={o="Speak with High Overlord Saurfang in Orgrimmar. He stands waiting for you in the Valley of Strength."},
[7785]={o="Examine the Vessel of Rebirth and return it to Highlord Demitrian."},
[7786]={o="To free Thunderaan the Windseeker from his prison, you must present the right and left halves of the Bindings of the Windseeker, 10 bars of Elementium, and the Essence of the Firelord to Highlord Demitrian in Silithus.",r={"Elementium Bar (10)","Essence of the Firelord (1)","Bindings of the Windseeker (1)","Bindings of the Windseeker (1)"}},
[7787]={o="Present the Dormant Wind Kissed Blade to Highlord Demitrian."},
[7790]={r={"Defeat Warsong Mill (1)"}},
[7791]={o="We are currently accepting donations for wool cloth. &nbsp;A donation of sixty pieces of wool cloth will net you full recognition by Stormwind for your generous actions. &nbsp;Our stores are such on wool that we would only need sixty pieces from you total; we should be able to acquire enough from others in the realm to support our drive. If you have the sixty pieces of wool cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.",r={"Wool Cloth (60)"}},
[7792]={o="We are currently accepting donations for wool cloth. &nbsp;A donation of sixty pieces of wool cloth will net you full recognition by Darnassus for your generous actions. &nbsp;Our stores are such on wool that we would only need sixty pieces from you total; we should be able to acquire enough from others in the realm to support our drive. If you have the sixty pieces of wool cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.",r={"Wool Cloth (60)"}},
[7793]={o="As with most other fabrics, our stocks of silk are at an all-time low. &nbsp;Our stores are such that we'd only need sixty pieces of silk from you total; we should be able to reach our goal with the support of others. A benevolent gift such as silk, might I add, would certainly increase your local standing in the community! &nbsp;If you have the sixty pieces of silk cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.",r={"Silk Cloth (60)"}},
[7794]={o="Mageweave is running low, and we could use your help to replenish our stocks! &nbsp;By counting on the community as a whole, we would only need a donation of 60 pieces of mageweave cloth from you to enable us to reach our goal. &nbsp;Such generosity would not go unnoticed by Stormwind, I assure you! If you have the sixty pieces of mageweave cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.",r={"Mageweave Cloth (60)"}},
[7795]={o="&lt;name&gt;, you've been a tremendous contributor to our cloth drive. &nbsp;As we work hard to replenish our reserves, one form of cloth remains critically low - runecloth. &nbsp;We are in absolutely dire need of it, and we hope that you will be able to help us as you have in the past! If you are willing, please bring me what runecloth you can spare. &nbsp;We'll initially accept a single donation of sixty, and then we'll go from there.",r={"Runecloth (60)"}},
[7796]={o="Greetings once again, &lt;name&gt;! &nbsp;Our need for runecloth is constant, and we can always use additional resources if you are willing to part with them. &nbsp;For an additional stack of twenty runecloth, I will make sure that you are recognized for your continuing efforts on behalf of Stormwind. Whenever you are ready to hand in the stack of runecloth, I'll accept it.",r={"Runecloth (20)"}},
[7798]={o="As with most other fabrics, our stocks of silk are at an all-time low. &nbsp;Our stores are such that we'd only need sixty pieces of silk from you total; we should be able to reach our goal with the support of others. A benevolent gift such as silk, might I add, would certainly increase your local standing in the community! &nbsp;If you have the sixty pieces of silk cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.",r={"Silk Cloth (60)"}},
